/* Lecture 10 video lecture data: parts, slide start times, timed bilingual transcript (generated). */
window.L10 = {"parts":[{"n":1,"title":"Why Multimodality?","blurb":"Why text alone is a narrow window onto the world: what a modality is, the character 聽, and why multimodality matters now.","file":"lecture10_part1.mp4","poster":"lecture10_part1.jpg","duration":445.6,"first":1,"last":10,"slides":[{"n":1,"title":"Title: Lecture 10, Multimodal LLMs","t":0.8},{"n":2,"title":"Before the lecture","t":20.76},{"n":3,"title":"Contents","t":79.42},{"n":4,"title":"1 Why Multimodality?","t":122.93},{"n":5,"title":"Even Listening Is Multimodal","t":142.42},{"n":6,"title":"What is Multimodality?","t":186.29},{"n":7,"title":"What is Multimodality?","t":253.92},{"n":8,"title":"What is Multimodality?","t":296.74},{"n":9,"title":"Why Multimodality?","t":333.79},{"n":10,"title":"Milestones","t":392.97}],"sents":[[0.8,3.24,1,"Hello everyone, and welcome back!","大家好，欢迎回来！"],[3.59,8.99,1,"Today is a really exciting one: Lecture ten, Multimodal Large Language Models.","今天这一讲非常精彩：第十讲，多模态大语言模型。"],[9.34,12.9,1,"So far in this course, our models could only read text.","到目前为止，我们的模型只会读文字。"],[13.25,18.16,1,"Today, we teach them to see, to hear, and even to act in the world.","今天，我们要教它们去看、去听，甚至在真实世界里行动。"],[18.51,19.36,1,"Let's go!","我们开始吧！"],[20.61,26.33,2,"Before we start the technical part, let me share a piece of good news from our own campus.","在进入技术部分之前，先和大家分享一个来自我们校园的好消息。"],[26.68,30.86,2,"This is a post from our president, Professor Yangsheng Xu.","这是我们校长徐扬生教授发的一条动态。"],[31.21,39.29,2,"A PhD student from our university co-founded a medical imaging startup called Cognita, and served as its CTO.","我们学校的一位博士生，作为 CTO 联合创办了一家医疗影像初创公司，叫 Cognita。"],[39.64,46.88,2,"And about a year ago, Cognita was acquired by Mosaic Clinical Technologies, for nearly one hundred million US dollars!","大约一年前，Cognita 以将近一亿美元的价格被 Mosaic Clinical Technologies 收购！"],[47.23,51.49,2,"So what did they build? Vision-language models for radiology.","他们做的是什么？面向放射科的视觉语言模型。"],[51.84,62.23,2,"Compared with radiologists working alone, their AI reduced major diagnostic errors by up to four times, and saved up to seventy-six percent of reading time.","和放射科医生单独阅片相比，他们的 AI 最多可把重大诊断错误减少四倍，阅片时间最多节省 76%。"],[62.58,68.27,2,"Think about it: a model that looks at a medical image, and writes the report like a doctor.","想一想：一个模型看一张医学影像，就能像医生一样写出报告。"],[68.62,73.74,2,"That is exactly the kind of multimodal model we are going to study today.","这正是我们今天要学习的多模态模型。"],[74.09,78.02,2,"So, join the journey on multimodal LLMs for society!","所以，欢迎一起加入“面向社会的多模态大模型”之旅！"],[79.27,81.55,3,"Here is our roadmap for today.","这是我们今天的路线图。"],[81.9,89.01,3,"We start with the foundations: why multimodality matters, and how vision meets language, with CLIP and Flamingo.","我们从基础开始：为什么多模态很重要，以及视觉如何与语言结合——CLIP 和 Flamingo。"],[89.36,95.32,3,"Then we build multimodal LLMs ourselves: the architecture, and how to train them.","然后我们自己搭建多模态大模型：它的架构，以及如何训练。"],[95.67,104.49,3,"And then we go beyond images: speech language models, generation and world simulators, embodied agents, and 3D.","接着我们超越图像：语音语言模型、生成与世界模拟器、具身智能，还有 3D。"],[104.84,107.06,3,"Now look at the bottom of the slide.","现在看一下幻灯片的底部。"],[107.41,116.27,3,"The story of today is simple: see, talk, hear and speak, imagine, act, and finally, understand space.","今天的故事很简单：看、说、听与讲、想象、行动，最后，理解空间。"],[116.62,121.53,3,"Six verbs. That is what a truly multimodal AI should be able to do.","六个动词。这就是一个真正的多模态 AI 应该具备的能力。"],[122.78,125.71,4,"Okay! Part one: why multimodality?","好！第一部分：为什么需要多模态？"],[126.06,129.8,4,"Think about how you are experiencing this lecture right now.","想一想你此刻是怎样在听这节课的。"],[130.15,134.86,4,"You see me, you hear my voice, you read the slides, all at the same time.","你看到我，听到我的声音，读着幻灯片，这一切同时发生。"],[135.21,141.02,4,"Text alone is a very narrow window onto a world full of images, sound, and motion.","只靠文字，就像透过一扇很窄的窗，去看一个充满图像、声音和运动的世界。"],[142.27,146.9,5,"Here is one of my favorite examples. Even listening is multimodal!","这是我最喜欢的例子之一：就连“听”都是多模态的！"],[147.25,152.13,5,"Look at this traditional Chinese character, ting, which means: to listen.","看这个繁体字“聽”，意思是：听。"],[152.48,155.16,5,"Of course, it contains an ear.","当然，它里面有一只“耳”。"],[155.51,158.79,5,"But it also contains an eye, and a heart.","但它还有一只“目”，和一颗“心”。"],[159.14,168.44,5,"So thousands of years ago, the people who created this character already knew: real listening uses your ears, your eyes, and your heart.","所以几千年前造这个字的人就已经知道：真正的倾听，要用耳朵、眼睛和心。"],[168.79,175.78,5,"And modern cognitive science agrees. The brain combines sound, vision, and language, all at once.","现代认知科学也同意：大脑会同时整合声音、视觉和语言。"],[176.13,180.31,5,"If humans understand the world this way, our AI should too.","既然人类是这样理解世界的，我们的 AI 也应该如此。"],[180.66,184.89,5,"And that is exactly why we need multimodal large language models.","这正是我们需要多模态大语言模型的原因。"],[186.14,192.27,6,"So what exactly do we mean by multimodality? Let's start with what it looks like in practice.","那么，多模态到底指什么？我们先看看它在实际中是什么样子。"],[192.62,199.97,6,"On the left, you see all the behaviors and signals that humans actually produce when they communicate.","左边列出了人类在交流时真正会产生的各种行为和信号。"],[200.32,204.41,6,"Language, of course: words, syntax, pragmatics.","当然有语言：词汇、句法、语用。"],[204.76,213.38,6,"But also acoustic signals like intonation and laughter, and visual signals like gestures, eye gaze, and facial expressions.","但还有声学信号，比如语调和笑声；以及视觉信号，比如手势、眼神和面部表情。"],[213.73,221.32,6,"And even touch, physiological signals like heart activity, and mobile sensors like GPS and accelerometers.","甚至还有触觉、心电这样的生理信号，以及 GPS、加速度计这样的移动传感器。"],[221.67,225.33,6,"Text is just one small box in this big picture!","文字只是这幅大图里的一个小方框！"],[225.68,229.86,6,"Now look at the right: a multimodal AI model for healthcare.","再看右边：一个用于医疗的多模态 AI 模型。"],[230.21,236.87,6,"It takes surgical images, a text note like: the patient developed heart failure, and photos with questions.","它接收手术影像、像“病人出现了心力衰竭”这样的文本记录，以及带提问的照片。"],[237.22,244.36,6,"All of them become tokens, get concatenated into one input, and go into a single multitask model.","所有这些都变成 token，拼接成一个输入，送进同一个多任务模型。"],[244.71,252.52,6,"So a user can ask: what caused this rash? And the AI answers: this is probably an allergic reaction.","于是用户可以问：这个皮疹是什么引起的？AI 回答：这很可能是过敏反应。"],[253.77,257.83,7,"Now let's be a bit more precise. Here's the definition.","现在我们说得更精确一点。这是定义。"],[258.18,262.32,7,"A modality is the way in which something is expressed or perceived.","模态，指的是某个东西被表达或被感知的方式。"],[262.67,267.75,7,"And here's a nice way to think about it: modalities live on a spectrum.","有一个很好的理解方式：模态分布在一条连续的谱上。"],[268.1,274.47,7,"On the left, raw modalities, closest to the sensor, like the speech signal or a raw image.","左边是原始模态，离传感器最近，比如语音信号或原始图像。"],[274.82,280.22,7,"As we move right, things get more abstract: language, and detected objects.","往右走，就越来越抽象：语言，以及检测出的物体。"],[280.57,288.57,7,"And at the far right, abstract modalities like sentiment intensity or object categories, farthest from the sensor.","最右边是抽象模态，比如情感强度或物体类别，离传感器最远。"],[288.92,295.34,7,"Notice where language sits: it is already a compressed, processed version of the world.","注意语言所处的位置：它已经是对世界的一种压缩和加工后的表示。"],[296.59,306.13,8,"Here's a fun fact about the word itself. Multimodal, as an adjective, means having several modes, modalities, or maxima.","关于这个词本身有个有趣的事实。multimodal 作为形容词，意思是具有多个模式、模态或极大值。"],[306.48,313.96,8,"In statistics, a multimodal distribution is one with several peaks, just like the 3D plot on the right.","在统计学里，多峰分布就是有好几个峰的分布，就像右边这张 3D 图。"],[314.31,317.4,8,"But in this course, we care about a different meaning.","但在这门课里，我们关心的是另一层含义。"],[317.75,327.01,8,"For us in NLP, multimodal means text plus one or more other modalities: images, speech, audio, even smell.","对我们 NLP 来说，多模态指的是文本加上一种或多种其他模态：图像、语音、音频，甚至气味。"],[327.36,332.39,8,"And today, we will mostly focus on images as the other modality.","今天，我们主要关注图像这一种其他模态。"],[333.64,339.28,9,"Okay, so why should we care? There is a whole range of very good reasons.","好，那我们为什么要关心多模态？有一系列非常好的理由。"],[339.63,347.06,9,"First, faithfulness. Human experience is multimodal: we see, hear, smell, taste, and touch.","第一，忠实性。人类的经验本身就是多模态的：我们看、听、闻、尝、触。"],[347.41,355.25,9,"Second, it is practical. The internet and so many real applications are full of images, videos, and audio.","第二，实用性。互联网和大量真实应用里都充满了图像、视频和音频。"],[355.6,358.85,9,"Third, data efficiency and availability.","第三，数据效率和可获得性。"],[359.2,362.16,9,"Multimodal data is rich and high bandwidth.","多模态数据信息丰富，带宽很高。"],[362.51,372.38,9,"Yann LeCun even called language an imperfect, incomplete, and low-bandwidth serialization protocol for the internal data structures we call thoughts.","Yann LeCun 甚至说，语言是我们称之为“思想”的内部数据结构的一种不完美、不完整、低带宽的序列化协议。"],[372.73,376.5,9,"So maybe learning from richer signals is simply better for learning.","所以，从更丰富的信号中学习，也许本身就更有利于学习。"],[376.85,382.38,9,"And scaling: more data is better, but we are running out of high-quality text data.","还有规模化：数据越多越好，但高质量的文本数据快要用完了。"],[382.73,386.06,9,"Images and videos are the next huge reservoir.","图像和视频就是下一个巨大的数据宝库。"],[386.41,391.57,9,"That's why multimodality is one of the main frontiers of the foundation model revolution.","这就是为什么多模态是基础模型革命的主要前沿之一。"],[392.82,398.21,10,"There are so many amazing multimodal systems today, so which ones should we study first?","如今有那么多出色的多模态系统，我们应该先学哪些？"],[398.56,406.11,10,"We start with two early milestones: CLIP from two thousand twenty-one, and Flamingo from two thousand twenty-two.","我们从两个早期的里程碑开始：2021 年的 CLIP 和 2022 年的 Flamingo。"],[406.46,412.59,10,"They are important, and their public details are clear, which makes them perfect for learning.","它们很重要，而且公开的细节很清楚，非常适合用来学习。"],[412.94,420.05,10,"CLIP was the first model that could generalize to many image classification tasks with zero-shot and few-shot learning.","CLIP 是第一个能以零样本和少样本学习泛化到多种图像分类任务的模型。"],[420.4,425.83,10,"Flamingo was not the first model to generate open-ended responses about images.","Flamingo 并不是第一个能针对图像生成开放式回答的模型。"],[426.18,433.2,10,"But its performance was so strong that some people called it the GPT-3 moment of the multimodal domain.","但它的表现非常强，以至于有人把它称为多模态领域的“GPT-3 时刻”。"],[433.55,437.93,10,"And building on them, we arrive at today's multimodal LLMs.","在它们的基础上，我们走到了今天的多模态大语言模型。"],[438.28,443.71,10,"So how do we actually connect vision and language? Let's start with CLIP.","那么，我们到底如何把视觉和语言连接起来？我们从 CLIP 开始。"]]},{"n":2,"title":"Connecting Vision and Language: CLIP and Flamingo","blurb":"Contrastive image-text pre-training at web scale, zero-shot classification, and Flamingo's resampler and gated cross-attention.","file":"lecture10_part2.mp4","poster":"lecture10_part2.jpg","duration":1173.9,"first":11,"last":35,"slides":[{"n":11,"title":"2 Connecting Vision and Language: CLIP and Flamingo","t":0.8},{"n":12,"title":"2.1 Early Work I: CLIP","t":20.57},{"n":13,"title":"CLIP: Contrastive Language-Image Pre-training","t":36.12},{"n":14,"title":"CLIP's high-level architecture","t":88.25},{"n":15,"title":"Scalable Data","t":145.18},{"n":16,"title":"Data Example: Wikipedia-based Image Text Dataset","t":205.27},{"n":17,"title":"An Even Larger One: LAION-5B","t":237.38},{"n":18,"title":"Existing Data","t":289.96},{"n":19,"title":"Discriminative vs. generative for image classifications","t":338.1},{"n":20,"title":"Contrastive objective (CLIP)","t":380.89},{"n":21,"title":"Contrastive objective (CLIP)","t":422.85},{"n":22,"title":"CLIP","t":469.49},{"n":23,"title":"CLIP applications: classification","t":526.1},{"n":24,"title":"CLIP applications: text-based image retrieval","t":579.28},{"n":25,"title":"CLIP applications: image generation","t":623.22},{"n":26,"title":"2.2 Early Work II: Flamingo","t":672.52},{"n":27,"title":"Flamingo: the dawns of LMMs","t":692.87},{"n":28,"title":"Flamingo's high-level architecture","t":743.23},{"n":29,"title":"Data","t":813.18},{"n":30,"title":"Flamingo's language model","t":889.36},{"n":31,"title":"Perceiver Resampler","t":922.88},{"n":32,"title":"GATED XATTN-DENSE layers","t":979.61},{"n":33,"title":"Loss function: autoregressive language models","t":1043.07},{"n":34,"title":"Flamingo Training","t":1086.92},{"n":35,"title":"CLIP vs. Flamingo","t":1106.87}],"sents":[[0.8,3.92,11,"Part two: connecting vision and language.","第二部分：连接视觉与语言。"],[4.27,9.3,11,"Two early ideas shaped every multimodal LLM you will see today.","有两个早期的想法，塑造了今天你会看到的每一个多模态大模型。"],[9.65,13.79,11,"First, CLIP teaches images and text to live in the same space.","第一，CLIP 让图像和文本生活在同一个空间里。"],[14.14,19.17,11,"Then Flamingo lets a language model actually talk about images. Let's dive in!","然后，Flamingo 让语言模型真正能够谈论图像。我们开始吧！"],[20.42,21.71,12,"Let's start with CLIP.","我们先从 CLIP 讲起。"],[22.06,28.6,12,"Here's the key idea: map images into the text space, using a contrastive objective.","核心思想是：用对比学习的目标，把图像映射到文本空间里。"],[28.95,34.72,12,"Simple, scalable, and still one of the best practices for aligning vision with language.","简单、可扩展，至今仍是对齐视觉与语言的最佳实践之一。"],[35.97,42.26,13,"CLIP stands for Contrastive Language-Image Pre-training, from OpenAI in two thousand twenty-one.","CLIP 的全称是对比式语言-图像预训练，由 OpenAI 在 2021 年提出。"],[42.61,48.3,13,"It combines two ingredients: natural language supervision, and contrastive learning.","它结合了两个要素：自然语言监督，以及对比学习。"],[48.65,53.84,13,"Together, they let CLIP scale up its data and make training much more efficient.","两者结合，让 CLIP 能够扩大数据规模，同时让训练更加高效。"],[54.19,59.15,13,"Now look at what this buys us on the right: zero-shot image classification.","再看右边，这带给我们的是：零样本图像分类。"],[59.5,67.82,13,"Show CLIP a photo of food, and it ranks guacamole first out of one hundred and one labels, with ninety point one percent.","给 CLIP 看一张食物照片，它在 101 个标签中把“牛油果酱”排在第一，概率是 90.1%。"],[68.17,73.53,13,"Show it an airplane, and again it picks the right answer, with eighty-nine percent.","给它看一架飞机，它同样选对了答案，概率是 89%。"],[73.88,79.77,13,"Notice the labels are just sentences, like a photo of a guacamole, a type of food.","注意，这些标签其实就是句子，比如“一张牛油果酱的照片，一种食物”。"],[80.12,86.85,13,"And nobody trained it on these datasets! So why and how do these two techniques work? Let's see.","而且没有人在这些数据集上训练过它！那么这两种技术为什么有效、又是如何起作用的？我们来看。"],[88.1,91.96,14,"Here is CLIP's high-level architecture. It has two towers.","这是 CLIP 的整体架构。它有两个塔。"],[92.31,99.14,14,"A piece of text, like happy hippie hamster, goes into a text encoder and becomes a text embedding.","一段文本，比如“happy hippie hamster”，进入文本编码器，变成一个文本向量。"],[99.49,106.07,14,"And the picture of the hamster goes into an image encoder and becomes an image embedding.","而这张仓鼠的图片进入图像编码器，变成一个图像向量。"],[106.42,110.76,14,"But these two embeddings have different sizes, so they live in different worlds.","但这两个向量的维度不同，它们处在不同的世界里。"],[111.11,119.16,14,"So each one is multiplied by a projection matrix, landing in one shared multimodal embedding space.","所以每个向量都乘上一个投影矩阵，落到同一个共享的多模态向量空间里。"],[119.51,124.94,14,"There, we simply compute a cosine similarity score between text and image.","在这个空间里，我们只需计算文本和图像之间的余弦相似度。"],[125.29,130.98,14,"Both encoders and both projection matrices are trained jointly, from scratch.","两个编码器和两个投影矩阵都是从零开始联合训练的。"],[131.33,138.92,14,"The goal: high similarity for the right image-text pairs, low similarity for the wrong ones. That is contrastive learning.","目标是：正确的图文对相似度高，错误的图文对相似度低。这就是对比学习。"],[139.27,143.78,14,"But to train this, you need a lot of image-text pairs. Where do they come from?","但要训练它，需要大量的图文对。它们从哪里来呢？"],[145.03,152.21,15,"For many years, image models were trained on manually annotated datasets, like ImageNet and MS COCO.","多年来，图像模型都是在人工标注的数据集上训练的，比如 ImageNet 和 MS COCO。"],[152.56,158.04,15,"But manual annotation is slow and expensive. It simply does not scale.","但人工标注又慢又贵，根本无法规模化。"],[158.39,167.29,15,"The CLIP authors found no existing dataset big enough and clean enough, so they built their own: four hundred million image-text pairs.","CLIP 的作者发现，现有数据集都不够大、不够好，于是自己构建了一个：四亿个图文对。"],[167.64,176.29,15,"Step one: build a list of five hundred thousand queries, from common words, bigrams, and popular Wikipedia titles.","第一步：构建五十万个查询，来自常用词、二元词组，以及热门维基百科条目的标题。"],[176.64,184.72,15,"Step two: find images matching these queries. The paper says not via search engines, so most likely an internal web crawl.","第二步：找到匹配这些查询的图像。论文说不是通过搜索引擎，所以很可能来自内部的网页抓取数据。"],[185.07,194.01,15,"Step three, and this is the clever part: pair each image with the text that naturally appears next to it, like captions or comments.","第三步，也是最巧妙的一步：把每张图像和它旁边自然出现的文本配对，比如图注或评论。"],[194.36,199.55,15,"Why not just the query? Because a query is too short to really describe the image.","为什么不直接用查询词？因为查询词太短了，无法真正描述图像。"],[199.9,203.87,15,"So the internet itself becomes the annotator, for free!","这样一来，互联网本身就成了免费的标注员！"],[205.12,211.54,16,"What does such web data look like? Here is a concrete example, a Wikipedia page about Half Dome.","这样的网络数据长什么样？这里有一个具体例子：一个关于半穹顶的维基百科页面。"],[211.89,217.48,16,"One page gives you many kinds of text for free: the page title, and the page description.","一个页面就能免费提供多种文本：页面标题，还有页面描述。"],[217.83,223.15,16,"And here is the image, with its own reference description right below it.","这里是图像，它正下方还有自己的说明文字。"],[223.5,228.53,16,"This is the idea behind WIT, the Wikipedia-based Image Text dataset.","这就是 WIT，也就是基于维基百科的图文数据集背后的思路。"],[228.88,235.98,16,"Every image comes with natural, human-written language around it. No extra labeling needed.","每张图像周围都有自然的、人类写的语言，不需要额外标注。"],[237.23,244.71,17,"And it gets even bigger. Meet LAION-5B, an open dataset with billions of image-text pairs.","规模还能更大。来看 LAION-5B，一个包含数十亿图文对的开放数据集。"],[245.06,251.19,17,"Each sample has an image URL, covering millions of domains, and a caption text.","每个样本都有一个图像 URL，覆盖数百万个域名，还有一段图注文本。"],[251.54,258.32,17,"Look at the similarity column: the cosine between image and text embeddings, computed with CLIP itself.","看相似度这一列：图像和文本向量之间的余弦相似度，正是用 CLIP 本身算出来的。"],[258.67,264.39,17,"So CLIP is now used to clean the data for the next generation of models. Nice loop, right?","所以，CLIP 现在被用来清洗下一代模型的数据。很妙的循环，对吧？"],[264.74,271.12,17,"There are also safety signals: the probability of a watermark, and the probability of unsafe content.","还有安全相关的信号：图像带水印的概率，以及内容不安全的概率。"],[271.47,277.27,17,"The data comes in three subsets: English, multilingual, and no detected language.","数据分为三个子集：英文、多语言，以及未识别出语言的部分。"],[277.62,283.54,17,"And notice the captions are short: on average sixty-seven, fifty-two, and forty-six.","注意这些图注都很短：平均长度分别是 67、52 和 46。"],[283.89,288.56,17,"Web text is short and noisy, but there is a huge amount of it.","网络文本又短又嘈杂，但数量极其庞大。"],[289.81,293.71,18,"Here is a snapshot of image datasets that exist today.","这是一份当今已有的图像数据集概览。"],[294.06,297.92,18,"The top half are open-source image-text datasets.","上半部分是开源的图文数据集。"],[298.27,305.0,18,"LAION-5B alone has five billion image-text pairs, about two hundred forty terabytes compressed.","仅 LAION-5B 就有五十亿个图文对，压缩后约 240TB。"],[305.35,315.59,18,"Then there are interleaved web documents like OBELICS and MMC4, and MINT-1T with two point six billion pairs.","还有 OBELICS、MMC4 这样的图文交错网页文档，以及有 26 亿图文对的 MINT-1T。"],[315.94,326.46,18,"The bottom half are commercial or domain datasets: art, photography, travel notes, recipes, and encyclopedias of species and plants.","下半部分是商用或领域数据集：艺术、摄影、游记、菜谱，以及生物和植物百科。"],[326.81,332.34,18,"The lesson: data is the fuel, and the community has collected a lot of it since CLIP.","启示是：数据就是燃料，自 CLIP 以来，社区已经积累了大量数据。"],[332.69,336.7,18,"Now, given all this data, what should the training objective be?","那么，有了这么多数据，训练目标应该是什么呢？"],[337.95,343.64,19,"Let's compare two ways to do image classification: discriminative and generative.","我们来比较图像分类的两种方式：判别式和生成式。"],[343.99,350.49,19,"Both start from a predetermined list of classes, like dog, cat, and so on.","两者都从一个预先确定的类别列表出发，比如狗、猫等等。"],[350.84,357.58,19,"A classifier outputs one probability distribution, and picks a single class. Here, cat.","分类器输出一个概率分布，然后选出一个类别。这里是“猫”。"],[357.93,363.7,19,"A language model does the same thing, but again and again: it outputs a sequence of classes.","语言模型做的是同样的事，只是一次又一次：它输出一个类别序列。"],[364.05,368.36,19,"So you get cat, and, dog, and so on.","于是你得到“猫”、“和”、“狗”，等等。"],[368.71,373.83,19,"Each generated class is a token, and the list of classes is simply the vocabulary.","每个生成的类别就是一个 token，而类别列表就是词表。"],[374.18,379.49,19,"So the generative way is much more flexible. Then why didn't CLIP just generate captions?","所以生成式要灵活得多。那 CLIP 为什么不直接生成图注呢？"],[380.74,383.7,20,"Here's the problem. Look at these two images.","问题在这里。看这两张图。"],[384.05,389.13,20,"Each one has five different human captions, and all of them are correct!","每张图都有五条不同的人工图注，而且全都是正确的！"],[389.48,396.18,20,"Several men in hard hats, or three men on a large rig. Same picture, very different words.","“几个戴安全帽的人”，或者“三个人在大型钻架上”。同一张图，用词却大不相同。"],[396.53,399.97,20,"So the texts for an image are diverse.","所以，一张图对应的文本是多样的。"],[400.32,405.56,20,"The CLIP authors found that a language model objective made training difficult.","CLIP 的作者发现，语言模型目标让训练变得困难。"],[405.91,416.07,20,"Their hypothesis: the model is forced to predict the exact text for each image, while many texts could fit, like alt-text, captions, or comments.","他们的假设是：模型被迫去预测每张图对应的精确文本，而其实很多文本都可以，比如替代文本、图注或评论。"],[416.42,421.45,20,"That is a much harder task than it needs to be. So how do we fix it?","这让任务变得比必要的难得多。那我们该如何解决？"],[422.7,424.81,21,"The answer is contrastive learning.","答案就是对比学习。"],[425.16,432.39,21,"Instead of predicting the exact text, CLIP only predicts whether a text is more likely to go with an image than other texts.","CLIP 不去预测精确的文本，而只判断：某段文本是否比其他文本更可能与这张图搭配。"],[432.74,441.07,21,"Take a batch of N image-text pairs. We get N image embeddings, V, and N text embeddings, L.","取一批 N 个图文对。我们得到 N 个图像向量 V，以及 N 个文本向量 L。"],[441.42,446.33,21,"Now compute the cosine similarity for all N squared possible pairings.","然后计算全部 N 平方个可能配对的余弦相似度。"],[446.68,453.13,21,"Only N of them are correct. Push those scores up, and push the other N squared minus N scores down.","其中只有 N 个是正确的。把它们的分数推高，把其余 N 平方减 N 个分数压低。"],[453.48,459.04,21,"And for CLIP, N is thirty-two thousand seven hundred sixty-eight!","而在 CLIP 中，N 等于 32768！"],[459.39,468.09,21,"That means every image is contrasted against more than thirty thousand texts in one step. Huge batches give lots of negatives.","这意味着每张图像在一步训练中要与三万多条文本做对比。大批量带来了大量负样本。"],[469.34,473.19,22,"Here is the famous CLIP figure, which puts everything together.","这是著名的 CLIP 示意图，把所有内容串在了一起。"],[473.54,481.59,22,"Part one, contrastive pre-training. Texts go through the text encoder, images go through the image encoder.","第一部分，对比预训练。文本经过文本编码器，图像经过图像编码器。"],[481.94,485.35,22,"This gives a grid of all image-text dot products.","这样就得到一个由所有图文点积组成的矩阵。"],[485.7,493.05,22,"The blue diagonal holds the correct pairs. Training pushes them up, and everything off the diagonal down.","蓝色对角线上是正确配对。训练会把它们推高，把对角线以外的全部压低。"],[493.4,500.1,22,"Part two: to build a classifier, take your label names, like plane, car, dog, and bird.","第二部分：要构建分类器，先拿出标签名，比如飞机、汽车、狗、鸟。"],[500.45,507.72,22,"Put each label into a prompt, a photo of a blank, and encode it with the text encoder.","把每个标签填进一个提示模板“一张……的照片”，再用文本编码器编码。"],[508.07,513.84,22,"Part three: encode a new image, and compare it against all those label embeddings.","第三部分：编码一张新图像，并与所有这些标签向量做比较。"],[514.19,517.28,22,"The best match wins: a photo of a dog.","最匹配的那个胜出：一张狗的照片。"],[517.63,524.7,22,"Notice what just happened. The text encoder became a classifier, with zero training examples. That is zero-shot!","注意刚刚发生了什么。文本编码器变成了分类器，而且一个训练样本都不需要。这就是零样本！"],[525.95,527.93,23,"So how good is zero-shot CLIP?","那么，零样本 CLIP 到底有多好？"],[528.28,537.26,23,"This chart compares zero-shot CLIP against a linear probe trained on ResNet-50 features, across twenty-seven datasets.","这张图在二十七个数据集上，把零样本 CLIP 和基于 ResNet-50 特征训练的线性探针做了比较。"],[537.61,546.66,23,"Green means CLIP wins. On StanfordCars it gains twenty-eight point nine points, and on Food101, twenty-two point five.","绿色表示 CLIP 胜出。在 StanfordCars 上它高出 28.9 个点，在 Food101 上高出 22.5 个点。"],[547.01,553.47,23,"Even on ImageNet it wins, by one point nine, without seeing a single ImageNet training label.","即使在 ImageNet 上它也赢了 1.9 个点，而且没见过任何一个 ImageNet 训练标签。"],[553.82,558.53,23,"In total, it wins on sixteen of these twenty-seven datasets.","总的来说，它在这二十七个数据集中的十六个上胜出。"],[558.88,569.48,23,"Blue means CLIP loses, on specialized tasks like satellite images in EuroSAT, distance estimation in KITTI, or digits in MNIST.","蓝色表示 CLIP 落后，主要是一些专门任务，比如 EuroSAT 的卫星图像、KITTI 的距离估计，或者 MNIST 的手写数字。"],[569.83,577.88,23,"Takeaway: for many classification tasks, CLIP is still a strong out-of-the-box baseline, used as-is or fine-tuned.","结论是：在很多分类任务上，CLIP 至今仍是一个强大的开箱即用基线，可以直接用，也可以微调。"],[579.13,582.58,24,"A second application: text-based image retrieval.","第二个应用：基于文本的图像检索。"],[582.93,590.52,24,"CLIP's training is basically retrieval in disguise: match images to texts, and texts to images.","CLIP 的训练本质上就是一种检索：图像匹配文本，文本匹配图像。"],[590.87,598.35,24,"The paper says it shows significant promise for image search, but admits it is noticeably below the state of the art there.","论文说它在图像搜索上展现出很大潜力，但也承认它明显低于该领域的最先进水平。"],[598.7,603.72,24,"Still, people use it. The clip-retrieval package is a good example.","尽管如此，大家还是在用它。clip-retrieval 工具包就是一个很好的例子。"],[604.07,609.67,24,"First, embed all your images with CLIP and store them in a vector database.","第一步，用 CLIP 编码所有图像，并存入向量数据库。"],[610.02,616.96,24,"Then embed the text query, and look up the images whose embeddings are closest to it.","然后编码文本查询，查找向量与它最接近的图像。"],[617.31,621.82,24,"Simple, fast, and it works with any words you like.","简单、快速，而且你想用什么词都可以。"],[623.07,625.87,25,"And a third application: image generation.","第三个应用：图像生成。"],[626.22,630.88,25,"Start from a prompt: a corgi playing a flame throwing trumpet.","从一个提示词开始：一只柯基在吹喷火的小号。"],[631.23,638.99,25,"Above the dotted line is CLIP training: the text encoder and image encoder are aligned by the CLIP objective.","虚线上方是 CLIP 的训练：文本编码器和图像编码器通过 CLIP 目标对齐。"],[639.34,644.9,25,"Below the line, a prior turns the text embedding into a CLIP image embedding.","虚线下方，一个先验模块把文本向量转换成 CLIP 图像向量。"],[645.25,649.56,25,"Then a decoder turns that image embedding into an actual picture.","然后，一个解码器把这个图像向量变成一张真实的图片。"],[649.91,656.2,25,"This is the design behind DALL-E 2. CLIP's shared space becomes the bridge from words to pixels.","这就是 DALL-E 2 背后的设计。CLIP 的共享空间成了从文字通往像素的桥梁。"],[656.55,664.59,25,"But notice what CLIP itself cannot do: it can match and rank, but it cannot write a single word about an image.","但请注意 CLIP 本身做不到什么：它能匹配、能排序，却无法为一张图像写出哪怕一个字。"],[664.94,671.12,25,"So how do we get a language model to look at images and generate text? That brings us to Flamingo.","那么，怎样让语言模型看着图像生成文字呢？这就引出了 Flamingo。"],[672.37,676.06,26,"Now, the second piece of early work: Flamingo.","现在来看第二项早期工作：Flamingo。"],[676.41,682.51,26,"CLIP could match images and text, but it could not say a single word about an image.","CLIP 能把图像和文字匹配起来，但它没法对一张图像说出哪怕一个词。"],[682.86,691.47,26,"Flamingo changes that: it lets a generative language model actually talk about images, and that is the dawn of large multimodal models.","Flamingo 改变了这一点：它让一个生成式语言模型真正“谈论”图像，这就是大型多模态模型的黎明。"],[692.72,695.49,27,"So what is Flamingo, in one line?","那么，用一句话说，Flamingo 是什么？"],[695.84,702.34,27,"In a reductive view, Flamingo equals CLIP plus an autoregressive language model.","简单粗暴地看，Flamingo 等于 CLIP 加上一个自回归语言模型。"],[702.69,711.09,27,"Here's the key difference: by adding a decoder language model, Flamingo can generate text responses, which CLIP simply cannot do.","关键区别在这里：加上一个解码器语言模型之后，Flamingo 能生成文本回答，而 CLIP 根本做不到。"],[711.44,715.67,27,"And the image encoder and the language model interact through attention.","而且图像编码器和语言模型之间通过注意力进行交互。"],[716.02,721.21,27,"Look at these conversations. You can ask about a dog: what breed is it, is it running?","看看这些对话。你可以问关于一只狗的问题：它是什么品种？它在跑吗？"],[721.56,728.91,27,"You can ask which city a street sign is in, play the Stroop color test, or compare a triangle with a hexagon.","你可以问一个路牌是在哪座城市，可以玩 Stroop 颜色测试，还可以比较三角形和六边形。"],[729.26,736.57,27,"In every case, Flamingo generates text conditioned on both the text and the images, in a multi-turn dialogue.","在每个例子里，Flamingo 都是同时以文本和图像为条件来生成文字，而且是多轮对话。"],[736.92,741.83,27,"That is a huge step beyond retrieval. So how is it built? Let's open the box.","这比单纯的检索前进了一大步。那它是怎么搭起来的？我们打开看看。"],[743.08,746.21,28,"Here is the high-level architecture of Flamingo.","这是 Flamingo 的整体架构。"],[746.56,756.02,28,"The input is interleaved visual and text data, like a picture of a dog, some text, then a picture of a cat, then more text.","输入是图文交错的数据，比如一张狗的照片、一段文字，然后一张猫的照片，再接着一段文字。"],[756.37,762.22,28,"Each image goes through a vision encoder, which is pretrained and frozen; see the little snowflake.","每张图像都会经过一个视觉编码器，它是预训练好并冻结的，看这个小雪花标志。"],[762.57,769.56,28,"Then a Perceiver Resampler, trained from scratch, turns the visual features into a small set of visual tokens.","然后一个从头训练的 Perceiver Resampler，把视觉特征转换成一小组视觉 token。"],[769.91,776.12,28,"On the right, the text is processed, with special image tags marking where each picture appears.","右边是处理后的文本，用特殊的 image 标记来表示每张图片出现的位置。"],[776.47,784.47,28,"The language model blocks are frozen, and between them we insert new GATED XATTN-DENSE layers that look at the visual tokens.","语言模型的各个模块是冻结的，在它们之间我们插入新的 GATED XATTN-DENSE 层，去关注视觉 token。"],[784.82,789.08,28,"And the output is just text: a very serious cat.","而输出就是文本：一只非常严肃的猫。"],[789.43,797.88,28,"So, two parts: a CLIP-like vision encoder trained contrastively, whose text encoder is then thrown away.","所以，一共两部分：一个用对比学习训练的类 CLIP 视觉编码器，训练完后它的文本编码器就被丢掉了。"],[798.23,806.77,28,"And a Chinchilla language model, extended with two new components: the Perceiver Resampler and the gated cross-attention layers.","以及一个 Chinchilla 语言模型，再加上两个新组件：Perceiver Resampler 和门控交叉注意力层。"],[807.12,811.78,28,"Before we zoom into those components, let's look at what data feeds this model.","在放大看这些组件之前，我们先看看喂给这个模型的是什么数据。"],[813.03,823.39,29,"Flamingo used four datasets: two image-text pair datasets, one video-text pair dataset, and one interleaved image and text dataset.","Flamingo 用了四个数据集：两个图文对数据集，一个视频-文本对数据集，以及一个图文交错数据集。"],[823.74,828.77,29,"Image-text pairs are what we saw with CLIP: a picture and its caption.","图文对就是我们在 CLIP 里见过的：一张图片加上它的描述。"],[829.12,834.19,29,"Video-text pairs add time, like a kid doing a kickflip.","视频-文本对加入了时间维度，比如一个孩子在做滑板翻板动作。"],[834.54,844.17,29,"And the new one is M3W, the MultiModal MassiveWeb dataset: real webpages where images and text are mixed together.","而新的是 M3W，也就是多模态海量网页数据集：图像和文字混排在一起的真实网页。"],[844.52,855.24,29,"Look at the table: M3W has forty-three million webpages, and from each page they sample two hundred fifty-six tokens with up to five images.","看这个表：M3W 有四千三百万个网页，每个网页采样 256 个 token，最多包含 5 张图片。"],[855.59,864.77,29,"ALIGN has one point eight billion pairs with short alt-texts, and LTIP has three hundred twelve million pairs with longer descriptions.","ALIGN 有 18 亿个图文对，文本是简短的 alt 文本；LTIP 有 3.12 亿个图文对，描述更长。"],[865.12,870.48,29,"VTP has twenty-seven million short videos, about twenty-two seconds each.","VTP 有两千七百万个短视频，平均每个大约 22 秒。"],[870.83,878.18,29,"Notice the training weights: the interleaved M3W data gets weight one point zero, much more than the others.","注意训练权重：图文交错的 M3W 数据权重是 1.0，比其他数据集高得多。"],[878.53,887.96,29,"Why does that matter? Interleaved data teaches the model to read several images and texts in one sequence, which is exactly what few-shot prompting needs.","这为什么重要？交错数据教会模型在一个序列里读多张图和多段文字，而这正是小样本提示所需要的。"],[889.21,891.03,30,"Now the language model itself.","现在来看语言模型本身。"],[891.38,896.45,30,"Flamingo uses Chinchilla, and the pretrained Chinchilla layers are kept frozen.","Flamingo 使用 Chinchilla，并且预训练好的 Chinchilla 层保持冻结。"],[896.8,901.71,30,"A traditional language model predicts the next text token from the preceding text tokens.","传统的语言模型根据前面的文本 token 预测下一个文本 token。"],[902.06,908.08,30,"Flamingo predicts the next text token from both the preceding text and the visual tokens.","Flamingo 则是同时根据前面的文本和视觉 token 来预测下一个文本 token。"],[908.43,914.35,30,"So the images become part of the context, but the model still only outputs text.","所以图像成为了上下文的一部分，但模型输出的仍然只有文字。"],[914.7,921.48,30,"But wait: how do we turn images into a neat set of visual tokens? That's the Perceiver Resampler.","但等一下：怎么把图像变成一组整齐的视觉 token 呢？这就要靠 Perceiver Resampler。"],[922.73,927.8,31,"Here's the problem: the visual input can be a single image or a whole video.","问题在于：视觉输入可能是一张图片，也可能是一整段视频。"],[928.15,934.28,31,"So the vision encoder produces a variable number of features, one grid per frame.","所以视觉编码器会产生数量不固定的特征，每一帧一个特征网格。"],[934.63,940.65,31,"We add time embeddings for each frame, and flatten everything into one long sequence of features.","我们给每一帧加上时间嵌入，然后把所有特征展平成一个长序列。"],[941.0,945.26,31,"Now here's the trick: a small set of learned latent queries.","现在关键技巧来了：一小组可学习的潜在查询。"],[945.61,953.69,31,"These latents act as the queries, and the visual features act as keys and values in attention, followed by a feed-forward layer.","这些潜在向量作为查询，视觉特征作为注意力里的键和值，后面再接一个前馈层。"],[954.04,962.65,31,"Because the number of queries is fixed, the output size is fixed too: always sixty-four visual tokens, no matter how long the video is.","因为查询的数量是固定的，输出大小也就固定了：无论视频多长，始终是 64 个视觉 token。"],[963.0,970.27,31,"The code on the right is short: for each layer, attention, then feed-forward, both with residual connections.","右边的代码很短：每一层先做注意力，再做前馈，两者都带残差连接。"],[970.62,978.21,31,"Think of it as a compressor that summarizes any visual input into a fixed budget of tokens for the language model.","你可以把它看成一个压缩器，把任意视觉输入总结成固定数量的 token，交给语言模型。"],[979.46,986.94,32,"So how does the frozen language model actually look at these visual tokens? With GATED XATTN-DENSE layers.","那么冻结的语言模型到底怎么“看”这些视觉 token 呢？靠的是 GATED XATTN-DENSE 层。"],[987.29,993.14,32,"These new layers are inserted between the existing, frozen LM layers.","这些新层被插入到原有的、冻结的语言模型层之间。"],[993.49,1001.54,32,"Zoom in: first comes cross-attention, where the queries come from the language, and the keys and values come from the vision features.","放大来看：首先是交叉注意力，查询来自语言，键和值来自视觉特征。"],[1001.89,1009.53,32,"Then a dense feed-forward layer, and after that the original frozen self-attention and feed-forward layers.","然后是一个稠密的前馈层，之后才是原来冻结的自注意力层和前馈层。"],[1009.88,1018.64,32,"Here's the clever part: each new branch is multiplied by tanh of a gate parameter, alpha, which is initialized at zero.","巧妙之处在于：每个新分支都乘上一个门控参数 alpha 的 tanh，而 alpha 初始化为零。"],[1018.99,1024.88,32,"Tanh of zero is zero, so at the start the language model behaves exactly like the original Chinchilla.","tanh 零等于零，所以一开始语言模型的行为和原来的 Chinchilla 完全一样。"],[1025.23,1033.03,32,"Then, during training, the gates slowly open and visual information flows in, which keeps training stable.","然后在训练中，门慢慢打开，视觉信息逐渐流入，这让训练保持稳定。"],[1033.38,1041.67,32,"And it matters: according to the ablation quoted here, without this design the overall score drops by four point two percent.","而且这很重要：根据这里引用的消融实验，去掉这个设计，总体得分会下降 4.2%。"],[1042.92,1050.15,33,"Now, what is the training objective? Good news: it's our old friend, the autoregressive language modeling loss.","那么训练目标是什么？好消息：就是我们的老朋友，自回归语言建模损失。"],[1050.5,1058.39,33,"Flamingo computes the likelihood of the text y, conditioned on the interleaved images and videos x.","Flamingo 计算文本 y 在图文交错的图像和视频 x 条件下的似然。"],[1058.74,1066.46,33,"It's a product over tokens: each text token depends on the previous text tokens and on the images that came before it.","它是对每个 token 的连乘：每个文本 token 依赖于前面的文本 token，以及在它之前出现的图像。"],[1066.81,1072.69,33,"The training loss is a weighted sum of negative log-likelihoods across all four datasets.","训练损失是在全部四个数据集上的负对数似然的加权和。"],[1073.04,1079.78,33,"And lambda m is the weight of dataset m, exactly the training weights we saw in the data table.","而 lambda m 是数据集 m 的权重，正是我们在数据表里看到的那些训练权重。"],[1080.13,1085.52,33,"So no new magic in the loss. All the novelty is in the architecture and the data.","所以损失函数里没有什么新魔法，所有的创新都在架构和数据上。"],[1086.77,1090.92,34,"One practical note: Flamingo itself was never open-sourced.","一个实际的提醒：Flamingo 本身从未开源。"],[1091.27,1099.03,34,"But the community built open replications, like IDEFICS from Hugging Face, and OpenFlamingo from mlfoundations.","但社区做了开源复现，比如 Hugging Face 的 IDEFICS，以及 mlfoundations 的 OpenFlamingo。"],[1099.38,1105.47,34,"If you want to play with a Flamingo-style model in your project, these are great starting points.","如果你想在项目里玩一玩 Flamingo 式的模型，这些都是很好的起点。"],[1106.72,1110.74,35,"Let's wrap up this part by putting CLIP and Flamingo side by side.","我们把 CLIP 和 Flamingo 放在一起对比，来总结这一部分。"],[1111.09,1120.03,35,"Data: CLIP used four hundred million image-text pairs, while Flamingo mixed four datasets, including interleaved webpages.","数据：CLIP 用了四亿个图文对，而 Flamingo 混合了四个数据集，其中包括图文交错的网页。"],[1120.38,1128.83,35,"Both train a vision encoder with the same contrastive objective; Flamingo uses an NFNet, and then freezes it.","两者都用相同的对比学习目标来训练视觉编码器；Flamingo 用的是 NFNet，训练完就冻结。"],[1129.18,1136.12,35,"And Flamingo's text encoder, a BERT, is used only for that contrastive step and then discarded.","Flamingo 的文本编码器是 BERT，只用于对比学习这一步，之后就被丢弃。"],[1136.47,1140.41,35,"But look at the last row: CLIP has no language model at all.","但看最后一行：CLIP 根本没有语言模型。"],[1140.76,1151.0,35,"Flamingo adds a frozen Chinchilla, a Perceiver Resampler with sixty-four visual tokens, and gated cross-attention layers trained from scratch.","Flamingo 加入了冻结的 Chinchilla、输出 64 个视觉 token 的 Perceiver Resampler，以及从头训练的门控交叉注意力层。"],[1151.35,1157.68,35,"That is the real leap: from matching images and text, to generating language about images.","这才是真正的飞跃：从匹配图像和文字，到针对图像生成语言。"],[1158.03,1164.89,35,"So, frozen vision encoder, a connector, and a powerful language model: keep this recipe in mind.","所以：冻结的视觉编码器、一个连接模块，再加一个强大的语言模型，请记住这个配方。"],[1165.24,1172.1,35,"Because next, we'll see how modern multimodal LLMs are built on exactly this idea. Let's go!","因为接下来，我们就会看到现代多模态大模型正是基于这个思路搭建的。我们继续！"]]},{"n":3,"title":"Multimodal LLMs: Architecture","blurb":"Language as the pivot, LLM-as-controller versus joint models, and how images and other modalities enter an LLM.","file":"lecture10_part3.mp4","poster":"lecture10_part3.jpg","duration":1149.1,"first":36,"last":62,"slides":[{"n":36,"title":"3 Multimodal LLMs: Architecture","t":0.8},{"n":37,"title":"Multimodal LLMs","t":28.01},{"n":38,"title":"Multimodal LLMs","t":51.21},{"n":39,"title":"Preliminary Idea: Intelligence over Language","t":90.1},{"n":40,"title":"Preliminary Idea: Language Intelligence as Pivot","t":118.34},{"n":41,"title":"Language for communication and also thought","t":160.17},{"n":42,"title":"Type-I: LLM as Discrete Scheduler/Controller","t":214.05},{"n":43,"title":"Type-I: LLM as Discrete Scheduler/Controller","t":251.65},{"n":44,"title":"Type-I: LLM as Discrete Scheduler/Controller","t":273.3},{"n":45,"title":"Type-II: LLM as Joint Part of System","t":329.46},{"n":46,"title":"Architecture of LLMs","t":382.61},{"n":47,"title":"LLaVA: Large Language-and-Vision Assistant","t":401.01},{"n":48,"title":"Other Multimodal LLMs: Qwen-VL","t":454.79},{"n":49,"title":"Other Multimodal LLMs: CogVLM-Chat","t":498.92},{"n":50,"title":"Other Multimodal LLMs: Fuyu","t":542.79},{"n":51,"title":"Native Multimodal Models: GPT-4o & Gemini","t":581.41},{"n":52,"title":"Open-Source SOTA Multimodal LLMs","t":630.29},{"n":53,"title":"Unified Understanding and Generation","t":680.65},{"n":54,"title":"Visual encoders or tokenizer","t":745.97},{"n":55,"title":"Visual Encoder","t":763.67},{"n":56,"title":"Visual Encoder","t":813.09},{"n":57,"title":"Visual Encoder","t":854.44},{"n":58,"title":"Non-Visual Encoder","t":906.09},{"n":59,"title":"Unified Multimodal Encoder","t":944.27},{"n":60,"title":"Unified Multimodal Encoder","t":992.87},{"n":61,"title":"Tokenization","t":1032.13},{"n":62,"title":"Tokenization","t":1083.35}],"sents":[[0.8,5.39,36,"Welcome to Part three: the architecture of multimodal LLMs.","欢迎来到第三部分：多模态大语言模型的架构。"],[5.74,12.68,36,"We just saw how CLIP aligns images with text, and how Flamingo lets a language model look at images.","我们刚刚看到了 CLIP 如何把图像和文本对齐，以及 Flamingo 如何让语言模型看图。"],[13.03,24.08,36,"Now here is the big recipe: keep language as the pivot, encode the other modalities, project them into the LLM's token space, and let the LLM reason.","现在来看核心配方：以语言为枢纽，先编码其他模态，再把它们投影到大模型的词元空间，然后让大模型去推理。"],[24.43,26.61,36,"Let's see how this is actually built!","我们来看看它到底是怎么搭建起来的！"],[27.86,32.42,37,"First, a quick question: why build multimodal LLMs at all?","首先，一个简单的问题：我们为什么要做多模态大模型？"],[32.77,35.36,37,"Welcome to the era of large language models.","欢迎来到大语言模型的时代。"],[35.71,41.51,37,"Large language models really improved cognition-level abilities, like reasoning and planning.","大语言模型确实大大提升了认知层面的能力，比如推理和规划。"],[41.86,49.81,37,"But on their own, they only read and write text, so they cannot directly see the world. That is the gap we want to close.","但仅靠它们自己，只能读写文字，没法直接看见这个世界。这正是我们要弥补的缺口。"],[51.06,57.03,38,"So what does a multimodal LLM look like in action? Here is a chat with LLaVA.","那么，多模态大模型实际用起来是什么样？这是和 LLaVA 的一段对话。"],[57.38,64.04,38,"The user uploads a screenshot and asks: what is written, and who could be interested in this content?","用户上传了一张截图，然后问：上面写了什么？谁会对这些内容感兴趣？"],[64.39,65.57,38,"Look at the answer.","看看它的回答。"],[65.92,73.84,38,"The model describes the city skyline and the sunset, and it reads the text: recent advances in vision foundation models.","模型描述了城市天际线和日落，还读出了图里的文字：视觉基础模型的最新进展。"],[74.19,82.95,38,"Then it goes one step further and reasons that researchers in computer vision and AI might care, and that it is probably a conference event.","接着它更进一步推理：计算机视觉和人工智能方向的研究者可能会感兴趣，而且这很可能是一个会议活动。"],[83.3,88.7,38,"So it sees, it reads, and it reasons, all in one conversation.","所以它能看、能读、还能推理，全都在一次对话里完成。"],[89.95,94.18,39,"Here is the preliminary idea behind almost all of these systems.","几乎所有这些系统背后，都有一个基本想法。"],[94.53,100.66,39,"Emergent phenomena have already shown up extensively in language-based LLMs.","在基于语言的大模型中，涌现现象已经大量出现了。"],[101.01,105.31,39,"These models now have very powerful semantic understanding capabilities.","这些模型现在普遍拥有非常强大的语义理解能力。"],[105.66,111.71,39,"And that tells us something deep: language is a crucial modality for carrying intelligence.","这告诉我们一件很深刻的事：语言是承载智能的关键模态。"],[112.06,116.94,39,"So if the intelligence already lives in language, why not build on top of it?","既然智能已经存在于语言之中，为什么不在它之上继续搭建呢？"],[118.19,121.2,40,"And that is exactly what the field did.","这正是整个领域的做法。"],[121.55,130.49,40,"Nearly all current multimodal LLMs use a language-based LLM as the core decision-making module, the brain, or the central processor.","几乎所有当前的多模态大模型，都以基于语言的大模型作为核心决策模块，也就是大脑，或者说中央处理器。"],[130.84,135.06,40,"Then we add external modules for the non-textual modalities.","然后，我们再为非文本模态加上外部模块。"],[135.41,144.3,40,"Look at the picture: visual, video, and 3D on the left, smell, sound, and touch on the right, all flowing into language in the middle.","看这张图：左边是视觉、视频和 3D，右边是嗅觉、声音和触觉，它们都汇入中间的语言。"],[144.65,148.8,40,"Language is the pivot, the hub that everything connects to.","语言就是枢纽，所有模态都连接到它这里。"],[149.15,158.77,40,"Why bother? It extends the capability boundary, it is the next milestone toward more advanced intelligence, and it opens up many more applications.","为什么要这么做？因为它扩展了能力边界，是迈向更高级智能的下一个里程碑，还能带来更多应用。"],[160.02,166.44,41,"But wait. Is language really the right pivot for intelligence? Let's pause on a little debate.","不过，等一下。语言真的是智能的合适枢纽吗？我们先停下来看一个小小的争论。"],[166.79,168.83,41,"Here is Noam Chomsky.","这位是诺姆·乔姆斯基。"],[169.18,180.62,41,"He argues that the purpose of language is not only communication; it is also used to express and clarify thought, for play, and to gain understanding.","他认为，语言的用途不只是交流；它还被用来表达和厘清思想、用来游戏，以及获得理解。"],[180.97,185.93,41,"In his view, there is no reason to give either mode a privileged status.","在他看来，没有理由让其中任何一种用途享有特殊地位。"],[186.28,195.82,41,"On the other hand, a recent perspective paper in Nature argues that language is primarily a tool for communication rather than thought.","另一方面，《自然》杂志上最近的一篇观点文章认为，语言主要是交流的工具，而不是思维的工具。"],[196.17,205.68,41,"So the question is still open. But in practice, language has turned out to be an extremely useful hub for today's models.","所以这个问题至今仍有争议。但在实践中，语言已经被证明是当今模型非常好用的枢纽。"],[206.03,212.65,41,"Now, given language as the pivot, there are two ways to connect the other modalities. Let's look at type one.","那么，以语言为枢纽，有两种方式把其他模态接进来。我们先看第一类。"],[213.9,218.57,42,"Type one: the LLM as a discrete scheduler, or controller.","第一类：大模型作为离散的调度器，或者说控制器。"],[218.92,225.78,42,"Here the LLM receives textual signals, and sends out textual commands to call downstream modules.","在这里，大模型接收文本信号，然后发出文本指令去调用下游模块。"],[226.13,232.58,42,"Follow the diagram: the user sends text to the LLM, and the LLM sends text to a set of downstream tools.","跟着这张图看：用户把文本发给大模型，大模型再把文本发给一组下游工具。"],[232.93,235.37,42,"The results then come back to the user.","然后结果再返回给用户。"],[235.72,244.21,42,"Here's the key feature: every message in the system, from encoder to LLM, or from LLM to tools, is pure text.","关键特点在这里：系统里的每一条消息，无论是编码器到大模型，还是大模型到工具，都是纯文本。"],[244.56,250.25,42,"The LLM never sees the pixels. It only reads and writes words.","大模型从来看不到像素，它只读写文字。"],[251.5,254.09,43,"Many well-known systems follow this design.","很多知名系统都采用了这种设计。"],[254.44,263.49,43,"Visual-ChatGPT, HuggingGPT, MM-REACT, ViperGPT, AudioGPT, and LLaVA-Plus, to name a few.","比如 Visual-ChatGPT、HuggingGPT、MM-REACT、ViperGPT、AudioGPT 和 LLaVA-Plus 等等。"],[263.84,269.32,43,"They all share the same loop: user, LLM, tools, and back to the user.","它们都有同样的循环：用户、大模型、工具，再回到用户。"],[269.67,271.9,43,"Let's look at two of them in more detail.","我们来更仔细地看其中两个。"],[273.15,275.59,44,"On the left is Visual ChatGPT.","左边是 Visual ChatGPT。"],[275.94,284.43,44,"The user asks for something complex, like generating a red flower from the depth of an image, and then making it a cartoon.","用户提了一个复杂的请求，比如根据图像的深度生成一朵红花，再把它变成卡通风格。"],[284.78,293.43,44,"A prompt manager lets ChatGPT call visual foundation models like BLIP, Stable Diffusion, and ControlNet, step by step.","一个提示管理器让 ChatGPT 一步一步地调用 BLIP、Stable Diffusion、ControlNet 等视觉基础模型。"],[293.78,300.15,44,"On the right is HuggingGPT, where the LLM is the controller and Hugging Face models are the tools.","右边是 HuggingGPT，大模型是控制器，Hugging Face 上的模型就是工具。"],[300.5,307.64,44,"It goes through four stages: task planning, model selection, task execution, and response generation.","它分四个阶段：任务规划、模型选择、任务执行和回复生成。"],[307.99,314.49,44,"The good news: it is quick to build, with no training, and you can flexibly plug in many tools.","好处是：搭建很快，不需要训练，还能灵活地接入很多工具。"],[314.84,321.58,44,"The bad news: everything is squeezed through text, so information gets lost. Text becomes the bottleneck.","坏处是：所有信息都要挤过文本这一关，所以会有信息损失。文本就成了瓶颈。"],[321.93,328.06,44,"Can a caption really capture every detail of an image? Of course not. So we need something better.","一段描述真的能涵盖图像的所有细节吗？当然不能。所以我们需要更好的方案。"],[329.31,334.79,45,"That brings us to type two: the LLM as a joint part of the system.","这就引出了第二类：大模型作为整个系统中联合的一部分。"],[335.14,339.97,45,"More than ninety percent of multimodal LLMs belong to this category.","超过百分之九十的多模态大模型都属于这一类。"],[340.32,345.51,45,"It has a higher upper bound, because everything is integrated into one unified model.","它的上限更高，因为一切都被整合进了一个统一的模型。"],[345.86,352.56,45,"Look at the pipeline: a modality encoder turns images, audio, or video into features.","看这条流水线：模态编码器把图像、音频或视频变成特征。"],[352.91,358.96,45,"A connector maps those features into tokens the LLM can read, right next to the text tokens.","连接器把这些特征映射成大模型能读的词元，和文本词元放在一起。"],[359.31,366.78,45,"The LLM reasons over all of them, and an optional generator can even produce images, audio, or video.","大模型对它们统一进行推理，还可以接一个可选的生成器，去生成图像、音频或视频。"],[367.13,376.43,45,"At the bottom, you see three common connectors: a simple MLP, a Q-Former with learnable queries, and cross-attention inside the LLM.","下方是三种常见的连接器：简单的 MLP、带可学习查询的 Q-Former，以及大模型内部的交叉注意力。"],[376.78,381.21,45,"Notice the last one: that is exactly the Flamingo style you saw earlier.","注意最后一种：这正是你之前看到的 Flamingo 的做法。"],[382.46,386.15,46,"Now let's open the box and look at real architectures.","现在我们打开黑盒，看看真实的模型架构。"],[386.5,394.95,46,"We will walk through LLaVA, Qwen-VL, CogVLM, and Fuyu, and then the newest native and unified models.","我们会依次看 LLaVA、Qwen-VL、CogVLM 和 Fuyu，然后再看最新的原生多模态和统一模型。"],[395.3,399.61,46,"Watch for one question every time: how does the image get into the LLM?","每次都请留意一个问题：图像是怎么进入大模型的？"],[400.86,406.5,47,"Let's start with LLaVA, the Large Language-and-Vision Assistant. It is beautifully simple.","我们从 LLaVA 开始，也就是大型语言与视觉助手。它简洁得很漂亮。"],[406.85,412.0,47,"The image goes into a vision encoder, which gives visual features Z v.","图像先进入视觉编码器，得到视觉特征 Z v。"],[412.35,421.12,47,"Then a projection matrix W maps them into H v, visual tokens in the same space as the word embeddings.","然后一个投影矩阵 W 把它们映射成 H v，也就是和词嵌入处于同一空间的视觉词元。"],[421.47,426.54,47,"These visual tokens sit right next to the language instruction tokens, H q.","这些视觉词元就紧挨着语言指令的词元 H q。"],[426.89,430.96,47,"The language model reads them all and generates the response.","语言模型读入所有这些词元，然后生成回答。"],[431.31,433.21,47,"Training has two stages.","训练分两个阶段。"],[433.56,440.47,47,"Stage one is feature alignment: only the projection matrix is updated, using a subset of CC3M.","第一阶段是特征对齐：只更新投影矩阵，用的是 CC3M 的一个子集。"],[440.82,448.9,47,"Stage two is end-to-end fine-tuning: both the projection and the LLM are updated, on visual chat data and Science QA.","第二阶段是端到端微调：投影矩阵和大模型都会更新，数据是视觉对话数据和 Science QA。"],[449.25,453.39,47,"One linear layer as the bridge, and it works surprisingly well!","只用一层线性层作为桥梁，效果却出奇地好！"],[454.64,457.93,48,"Next, Qwen-VL from Alibaba.","接下来是阿里巴巴的 Qwen-VL。"],[458.28,465.71,48,"Instead of a plain projection, it uses a cross-attention module with learnable query embeddings to compress the ViT features.","它没有用简单的投影，而是用一个带可学习查询向量的交叉注意力模块，来压缩 ViT 的特征。"],[466.06,471.66,48,"Now watch the fire and snowflake icons: fire means trainable, snowflake means frozen.","注意看火焰和雪花图标：火焰表示可训练，雪花表示冻结。"],[472.01,478.91,48,"Stage one is pretraining on image-text pairs at low resolution, with the LLM frozen.","第一阶段在低分辨率下用图文对做预训练，大模型保持冻结。"],[479.26,487.72,48,"Stage two is multi-task pretraining with high resolution and interleaved vision-language data, and now everything is trained.","第二阶段是多任务预训练，使用高分辨率和图文交错数据，这时所有模块都参与训练。"],[488.07,493.02,48,"Stage three is supervised fine-tuning on chat data, with the ViT frozen.","第三阶段是在对话数据上做有监督微调，这时 ViT 被冻结。"],[493.37,497.52,48,"So the lesson is: carefully choose what to train, and when.","所以启示是：要仔细选择训练哪些部分，以及什么时候训练。"],[498.77,502.67,49,"Now CogVLM, which takes a deeper approach.","接下来是 CogVLM，它走得更深一步。"],[503.02,512.4,49,"On the left, the input looks familiar: a ViT encoder plus an MLP adapter for the image, and word embeddings for the text.","左边的输入很眼熟：图像经过 ViT 编码器和 MLP 适配器，文本经过词嵌入。"],[512.75,517.46,49,"The two sequences are concatenated and fed into the language model.","两个序列拼接起来，送进语言模型。"],[517.81,521.38,49,"But look at the right side: this is the visual expert.","但看看右边：这就是视觉专家模块。"],[521.73,529.37,49,"Inside every Transformer block, image features get their own QKV matrix and their own FFN, separate from the text.","在每一个 Transformer 块里，图像特征都有自己独立的 QKV 矩阵和 FFN，和文本分开。"],[529.72,535.15,49,"Only the purple parts are trainable, so the original language model stays untouched.","只有紫色部分是可训练的，所以原来的语言模型保持不变。"],[535.5,541.39,49,"This gives vision deep fusion at every layer, without hurting the language ability.","这样视觉在每一层都能深度融合，又不会损害语言能力。"],[542.64,547.06,50,"And here is the most minimal design of all: Fuyu.","再来看最极简的设计：Fuyu。"],[547.41,550.26,50,"There is no separate vision encoder at all!","它根本没有单独的视觉编码器！"],[550.61,556.49,50,"The input image is cut into patches, and each patch goes through a simple linear projection.","输入图像被切成小块，每一块经过一个简单的线性投影。"],[556.84,562.28,50,"These patch embeddings go straight into the Transformer decoder, just like word tokens.","这些图块嵌入就像文字词元一样，直接送进 Transformer 解码器。"],[562.63,569.13,50,"Notice the newline tokens: they mark the end of each row of patches, so the model knows the image layout.","注意这些换行符词元：它们标记每一行图块的结束，让模型知道图像的布局。"],[569.48,574.91,50,"Then the text follows, and the model says: this is a Fuyu persimmon.","然后是文本，模型输出：这是一个富有柿。"],[575.26,580.01,50,"One decoder, images and text treated almost the same way.","一个解码器，图像和文本几乎被一视同仁。"],[581.26,587.15,51,"Now the newest trend: a paradigm shift from modular to native multimodal models.","现在来看最新的趋势：从模块化走向原生多模态的范式转变。"],[587.5,597.97,51,"GPT-4o from OpenAI, two thousand twenty-four, is an omni-model: text, image, audio, and video, natively, in one end-to-end architecture.","OpenAI 在二〇二四年推出的 GPT-4o 是一个全能模型：文本、图像、音频和视频，都在一个端到端架构里原生处理。"],[598.32,604.45,51,"Gemini 2.0 from Google is native multimodal from the ground up, not CLIP plus LLM stitching.","谷歌的 Gemini 2.0 从一开始就是原生多模态的，而不是把 CLIP 和大模型拼接起来。"],[604.8,612.55,51,"The key advantage? It removes the information bottleneck between the vision encoder and the LLM.","关键优势是什么？它消除了视觉编码器和大模型之间的信息瓶颈。"],[612.9,619.28,51,"And it enables real-time interaction, with voice, vision, and text all at once.","它还支持实时交互，语音、视觉和文本同时进行。"],[619.63,628.89,51,"The trend keeps going: Meta's Muse Spark, and Qwen3.5 as native multimodal agents.","这个趋势还在继续：Meta 的 Muse Spark，以及作为原生多模态智能体的 Qwen3.5。"],[630.14,633.88,52,"What about the open-source world? It is moving very fast too.","开源世界呢？同样发展得非常快。"],[634.23,641.95,52,"Qwen2.5-VL from Alibaba brings dynamic resolution, video understanding, and agent capabilities.","阿里巴巴的 Qwen2.5-VL 带来了动态分辨率、视频理解和智能体能力。"],[642.3,651.73,52,"InternVL2.5 from Shanghai AI Lab scales up to seventy-eight billion parameters, with strong OCR and document understanding.","上海人工智能实验室的 InternVL2.5 扩展到了七百八十亿参数，OCR 和文档理解能力很强。"],[652.08,658.74,52,"DeepSeek-VL2 uses a mixture-of-experts architecture for efficient multimodal reasoning.","DeepSeek-VL2 采用混合专家架构，实现高效的多模态推理。"],[659.09,666.2,52,"LLaVA-OneVision is one unified model for single images, video, and multi-image tasks.","LLaVA-OneVision 用一个统一模型处理单图、视频和多图任务。"],[666.55,674.35,52,"And MiniCPM-V 2.6 is edge-efficient, rivaling GPT-4V on mobile devices.","而 MiniCPM-V 2.6 主打端侧高效，在移动设备上能媲美 GPT-4V。"],[674.7,679.25,52,"So you can build on strong open models today, even on your own phone.","所以今天你就能基于强大的开源模型来开发，甚至在自己的手机上。"],[680.5,687.44,53,"Finally, can one model both understand images and generate them? That is the goal of unified models.","最后，一个模型能不能既理解图像、又生成图像？这正是统一模型的目标。"],[687.79,697.5,53,"Janus-Pro from DeepSeek decouples visual encoding for understanding and for generation, but keeps one unified Transformer backbone.","DeepSeek 的 Janus-Pro 把用于理解和用于生成的视觉编码解耦，但保留一个统一的 Transformer 主干。"],[697.85,707.6,53,"Emu3 from BAAI does next-token prediction for text, image, and video, all as discrete tokens, and it was published in Nature.","智源的 Emu3 把文本、图像和视频都变成离散词元，统一做下一个词元预测，这项工作发表在了《自然》上。"],[707.95,712.86,53,"Chameleon from Meta is an early-fusion, token-based multimodal model.","Meta 的 Chameleon 是一个早期融合、基于词元的多模态模型。"],[713.21,721.91,53,"Here's the key insight: understanding needs semantic features, while generation needs low-level detail, so they may want different encoders.","关键洞见在于：理解需要语义特征，而生成需要底层细节，所以两者可能需要不同的编码器。"],[722.26,730.5,53,"Our own work, ShareGPT-4o-Image, also explores this direction, and we will come back to it later in the lecture.","我们自己的工作 ShareGPT-4o-Image 也在探索这个方向，本讲后面还会再讲到。"],[730.85,738.36,53,"Notice how everything we saw today starts from the same place: how do we turn pixels into something the LLM can use?","注意，今天我们看到的所有模型都从同一个问题出发：怎样把像素变成大模型能用的东西？"],[738.71,744.57,53,"So let's zoom in on that first component: the visual encoder, or tokenizer.","所以，我们来聚焦第一个组件：视觉编码器，或者说视觉分词器。"],[745.82,750.97,54,"Here it is: the part that turns pixels into something a language model can digest.","就是它：把像素变成语言模型能“消化”的东西的那一部分。"],[751.32,760.05,54,"Should we use a continuous visual encoder, or a tokenizer that turns images into discrete tokens, just like words?","我们应该用连续的视觉编码器，还是用分词器把图像变成像单词一样的离散 token？"],[760.4,762.27,54,"Let's look at both options.","我们两种方案都来看一看。"],[763.52,769.33,55,"Let's start with the most common choice: CLIP-ViT, the vision transformer trained with CLIP.","先看最常见的选择：CLIP-ViT，也就是用 CLIP 方法训练的视觉 Transformer。"],[769.68,779.22,55,"Why is it so popular? Because CLIP was trained to match images with text, so its image features already live close to the text space.","为什么它这么受欢迎？因为 CLIP 是通过图文匹配训练出来的，它的图像特征本来就和文本空间很接近。"],[779.57,783.47,55,"That makes connecting it to a language model much easier.","这让它和语言模型的对接变得容易得多。"],[783.82,788.7,55,"It also scales well: more parameters and more data give you better features.","它的扩展性也很好：更多参数、更多数据，就能得到更好的特征。"],[789.05,794.53,55,"Look at this chart: zero-shot accuracy against model size, on a log scale.","看这张图：横轴是对数尺度的模型参数量，纵轴是零样本准确率。"],[794.88,798.57,55,"As the CLIP models get bigger, the accuracy keeps going up.","随着 CLIP 模型越来越大，准确率一路上升。"],[798.92,804.61,55,"And a newer option, SigLIP, is gaining popularity, because it is smaller and stronger.","还有一个更新的选择 SigLIP，正越来越流行，因为它更小、也更强。"],[804.96,811.69,55,"It replaces CLIP's softmax contrastive loss with a simple sigmoid loss on each image-text pair.","它把 CLIP 的 softmax 对比损失，换成了对每个图文对单独计算的简单 sigmoid 损失。"],[812.94,817.17,56,"But these pretrained ViTs have a real limitation.","但是这些预训练的 ViT 有一个实实在在的局限。"],[817.52,826.54,56,"They take a fixed, low-resolution, square input: two twenty-four by two twenty-four, or three thirty-six by three thirty-six pixels.","它们只接受固定的、低分辨率的正方形输入：224×224，或者 336×336 像素。"],[826.89,828.55,56,"Look at this street photo.","看这张街景照片。"],[828.9,833.81,56,"Squeeze it into a tiny thumbnail, blow it back up, and everything gets blurry.","把它压成一张小小的缩略图，再放大回来，一切都变模糊了。"],[834.16,838.31,56,"Can you read the shop signs? I can't, and neither can the model.","你能看清店铺的招牌吗？我看不清，模型也看不清。"],[838.66,843.48,56,"Low resolution encoding misses the fine-grained visual details.","低分辨率编码会丢掉细粒度的视觉细节。"],[843.83,851.07,56,"So high-resolution perception is essential, especially for OCR, reading text in images, documents and charts.","所以高分辨率感知至关重要，尤其是 OCR，也就是读取图片、文档和图表里的文字。"],[851.42,853.04,56,"So how do we fix it?","那么怎么解决呢？"],[854.29,857.82,57,"The popular answer is simple: slice the image.","流行的答案很简单：把图像切片。"],[858.17,863.65,57,"Take a high-resolution image, and split it into a grid of tiles, here two by two.","拿一张高分辨率图像，把它切成网格小块，这里是二乘二。"],[864.0,869.92,57,"Each tile is encoded separately by the same visual encoder, at the resolution it was trained on.","每个小块都用同一个视觉编码器、在它训练时的分辨率下单独编码。"],[870.27,875.51,57,"We also resize the whole image down and encode it, so the model keeps the global view.","我们还会把整张图缩小后再编码一次，让模型保留全局视野。"],[875.86,881.71,57,"Then all the visual tokens are flattened and fed into the LLM.","然后把所有视觉 token 展平，送进 LLM。"],[882.06,888.03,57,"Local details from the tiles, plus global context from the thumbnail. Best of both worlds!","小块提供局部细节，缩略图提供全局上下文，两全其美！"],[888.38,897.68,57,"Many models use this idea: GPT-4V, LLaVA-NeXT, MiniCPM-V, LLaVA-UHD, Monkey, and more.","很多模型都用了这个思路：GPT-4V、LLaVA-NeXT、MiniCPM-V、LLaVA-UHD、Monkey 等等。"],[898.03,904.69,57,"The price? More tiles means many more visual tokens, so the input sequence gets much longer.","代价是什么？小块越多，视觉 token 就越多，输入序列也会长得多。"],[905.94,909.15,58,"Of course, images are not the only modality.","当然，图像并不是唯一的模态。"],[909.5,914.69,58,"For audio, we have encoders like Whisper, AudioCLIP, HuBERT and BEATs.","音频方面，有 Whisper、AudioCLIP、HuBERT 和 BEATs 这样的编码器。"],[915.04,918.78,58,"For 3D point clouds, there is Point-BERT.","3D 点云方面，有 Point-BERT。"],[919.13,922.98,58,"On the right is Whisper, a sequence-to-sequence transformer.","右边是 Whisper，一个序列到序列的 Transformer。"],[923.33,929.14,58,"The audio is first turned into a log-Mel spectrogram, then processed by transformer encoder blocks.","音频先被转换成对数梅尔频谱图，再经过 Transformer 编码器模块处理。"],[929.49,935.45,58,"The decoder then predicts text tokens one by one, using cross attention to look at the audio.","然后解码器通过交叉注意力关注音频，逐个预测文本 token。"],[935.8,942.87,58,"Many audio LLMs keep just the encoder part and use its features, exactly like we use CLIP for images.","很多音频大模型只保留编码器部分，使用它的特征，就像我们用 CLIP 处理图像一样。"],[944.12,949.72,59,"Now, here is a more ambitious idea: why not one encoder space for all modalities?","接下来是一个更大胆的想法：为什么不让所有模态共用一个编码空间呢？"],[950.07,956.49,59,"ImageBind embeds all modalities into one joint representation space, centered on images.","ImageBind 把所有模态嵌入到同一个联合表示空间中，并以图像为中心。"],[956.84,963.91,59,"Look at the modalities: images and videos, text, audio, depth, thermal, and IMU motion data.","看这些模态：图像和视频、文本、音频、深度、热成像，还有 IMU 运动数据。"],[964.26,969.22,59,"The trick is that each modality only needs paired data with images.","诀窍在于：每个模态只需要和图像配对的数据。"],[969.57,976.75,59,"Web image-text pairs, depth sensor data, web videos with audio, thermal data, and egocentric videos.","网络图文对、深度传感器数据、带音频的网络视频、热成像数据，以及第一人称视角视频。"],[977.1,984.62,59,"Then alignment between other pairs, like audio and text, emerges for free, without any direct paired data.","这样一来，其他模态之间的对齐，比如音频和文本，就会“免费”涌现出来，不需要直接配对的数据。"],[984.97,991.47,59,"And well aligned representations make it easier for an LLM to understand all these modalities.","而对齐良好的表示，能让 LLM 更容易理解所有这些模态。"],[992.72,995.72,60,"LanguageBind flips this idea around.","LanguageBind 把这个思路反了过来。"],[996.07,1001.15,60,"Instead of images, it uses language as the center of the joint space.","它不以图像为中心，而是以语言作为联合空间的中心。"],[1001.5,1004.78,60,"Remember our theme? Language as the pivot!","还记得我们的主题吗？语言作为枢纽！"],[1005.13,1008.83,60,"On the left, a language encoder encodes the text.","左边，语言编码器对文本进行编码。"],[1009.18,1015.23,60,"On the right, there are encoders for video, infrared, depth, audio, and more.","右边是视频、红外、深度、音频等模态的编码器。"],[1015.58,1019.23,60,"Each of them is aligned to language with contrastive learning.","每个编码器都通过对比学习和语言对齐。"],[1019.58,1025.6,60,"Notice the icons: the language encoder stays frozen, while the other encoders are fine-tuned with LoRA.","注意这些图标：语言编码器保持冻结，其他编码器则用 LoRA 微调。"],[1025.95,1030.73,60,"And adding a new modality is easy: just bind one more encoder to language.","增加一个新模态也很容易：只要再把一个编码器绑定到语言上就行。"],[1031.98,1039.0,61,"So far, we have turned signals into continuous vectors. But there is another way: tokenization.","到目前为止，我们都是把信号变成连续向量。但还有另一条路：分词化。"],[1039.35,1045.89,61,"The idea is to represent multimodal signals as discrete tokens from a codebook, just like words in a vocabulary.","思路是用码本里的离散 token 来表示多模态信号，就像词表里的单词一样。"],[1046.24,1048.6,61,"Look at AnyGPT.","看看 AnyGPT。"],[1048.95,1055.53,61,"Speech, images and music each get their own tokenizer, which turns them into discrete tokens.","语音、图像和音乐各有自己的分词器，把它们变成离散 token。"],[1055.88,1063.19,61,"Now everything becomes one long token sequence, with special tokens marking where each modality starts and ends.","这样所有内容都变成一条长长的 token 序列，用特殊 token 标记每个模态的开始和结束。"],[1063.54,1070.13,61,"On the output side, de-tokenizers turn the generated tokens back into speech, images and music.","在输出端，反分词器把生成的 token 还原成语音、图像和音乐。"],[1070.48,1077.5,61,"Here's the key advantage: one unified model for both understanding and generation, all with next-token prediction.","关键优势在于：一个统一的模型同时完成理解和生成，全部靠下一个 token 预测。"],[1077.85,1081.95,61,"The very same objective we have used for language models all along.","这正是我们一直以来训练语言模型所用的同一个目标。"],[1083.2,1088.73,62,"Now, if we use a continuous encoder, how do we connect its features to the LLM?","那么，如果用连续编码器，我们怎样把它的特征接到 LLM 上？"],[1089.08,1094.72,62,"The goal is to project the visual representations into the LLM's semantic space.","目标是把视觉表示投影到 LLM 的语义空间中。"],[1095.07,1099.9,62,"The simplest way is a linear projection, as in the original LLaVA.","最简单的方法是线性投影，比如最初的 LLaVA。"],[1100.25,1109.35,62,"One small step up is a two-layer MLP, as in LLaVA-1.5, and it works surprisingly well.","再进一步就是两层 MLP，比如 LLaVA-1.5，效果出奇地好。"],[1109.7,1117.29,62,"Q-Former, from BLIP-2, uses a set of learnable queries to pull out a fixed number of visual tokens.","BLIP-2 的 Q-Former 用一组可学习的查询向量，提取出固定数量的视觉 token。"],[1117.64,1126.05,62,"The Perceiver Resampler, in Flamingo and Qwen-VL, follows a similar idea: compress many visual features into a few tokens.","Flamingo 和 Qwen-VL 里的 Perceiver Resampler 思路类似：把大量视觉特征压缩成少量 token。"],[1126.4,1134.2,62,"C-Abstractor, from HoneyBee, is another way to compress visual tokens while keeping local structure.","HoneyBee 的 C-Abstractor 是另一种压缩视觉 token 的方式，同时保留局部结构。"],[1134.55,1141.95,62,"And the bottom picture shows a different route: inject visual features directly inside the LLM through attention.","最下面的图展示了另一条路线：通过注意力把视觉特征直接注入 LLM 内部。"],[1142.3,1147.21,62,"In practice, the simple MLP has become a very popular default.","在实践中，简单的 MLP 已经成为非常流行的默认选择。"]]},{"n":4,"title":"Training Multimodal LLMs","blurb":"Visual instruction tuning, caption and instruction data, and multi-stage training recipes.","file":"lecture10_part4.mp4","poster":"lecture10_part4.jpg","duration":723.6,"first":63,"last":78,"slides":[{"n":63,"title":"4 Training Multimodal LLMs","t":0.8},{"n":64,"title":"Recap on Language Modeling","t":16.25},{"n":65,"title":"Instruction Tuning in LLM","t":66.39},{"n":66,"title":"Instruction Tuning in LLM","t":115.92},{"n":67,"title":"Instruction Tuning in LLM","t":150.86},{"n":68,"title":"Instruction Tuning in Multimodal LLM","t":195.47},{"n":69,"title":"GPT-assisted Visual Instruction Data Generation","t":238.26},{"n":70,"title":"MLLM Instruction Tuning Framework","t":291.48},{"n":71,"title":"Multi-stage training in Multimodal LLMs","t":353.65},{"n":72,"title":"Training Data","t":375.86},{"n":73,"title":"Pretraining Alignment Data (i.e. image caption)","t":426.23},{"n":74,"title":"Pretraining Alignment Data (i.e. image caption)","t":466.84},{"n":75,"title":"Instruction Tuning Data (visual QA)","t":510.6},{"n":76,"title":"The Typical Training Paradigm","t":567.91},{"n":77,"title":"Training Paradigms","t":621.3},{"n":78,"title":"Pretraining Paradigms","t":683.13}],"sents":[[0.8,3.65,63,"Part four: training multimodal LLMs!","第四部分：训练多模态大模型！"],[4.0,9.02,63,"Here's the whole recipe in one line: alignment first, instruction following second.","整套配方一句话就能概括：先对齐，再学会遵循指令。"],[9.37,14.85,63,"And remember this: data quality matters more than architecture. Let's see why.","还要记住：数据质量比模型架构更重要。我们来看看为什么。"],[16.1,20.17,64,"First, a quick recap of how language models evolved.","首先，快速回顾一下语言模型是如何演进的。"],[20.52,26.77,64,"GPT-2, then GPT-3, which brought in-context learning and chain-of-thought.","从 GPT-2 到 GPT-3，带来了上下文学习和思维链。"],[27.12,32.24,64,"Then ChatGPT and InstructGPT added the crucial piece: instruction following.","接着 ChatGPT 和 InstructGPT 补上了关键的一环：指令遵循。"],[32.59,37.34,64,"And GPT-4 went further, accepting images as input.","GPT-4 更进一步，可以接受图像输入。"],[37.69,40.05,64,"Now look at the multimodal row below.","现在看下面多模态这一行。"],[40.4,48.04,64,"We had CLIP and Flamingo, strong vision-language models, but they could not really follow instructions like a chatbot.","我们有 CLIP 和 Flamingo 这样强大的视觉语言模型，但它们没法像聊天机器人那样真正遵循指令。"],[48.39,53.3,64,"So here is the gap: instruction following for multimodal models.","所以缺口就在这里：多模态模型的指令遵循。"],[53.65,60.79,64,"How do we get from CLIP to a multimodal GPT-4? That is the question for alignment research.","怎样从 CLIP 走到多模态的 GPT-4？这正是对齐研究要回答的问题。"],[61.14,64.99,64,"If you need a refresher, go back to lectures three and five.","如果需要复习，可以回看第三讲和第五讲。"],[66.24,71.03,65,"So what exactly is instruction tuning? Let's look at how we used to do NLP tasks.","那么指令微调到底是什么？我们先看看过去是怎么做 NLP 任务的。"],[71.38,77.07,65,"For translation, the input is Hello, Vancouver, and the output is its Chinese translation.","翻译任务：输入是 Hello, Vancouver，输出是它的中文翻译。"],[77.42,85.71,65,"For summarization, the input is a long paragraph about CVPR, and the output is a short summary.","摘要任务：输入是一段关于 CVPR 的长文字，输出是一句简短的摘要。"],[86.06,92.64,65,"But notice: nobody tells the model which task to do. The task instructions are implicit.","但请注意：没有人告诉模型要做哪个任务，任务指令是隐含的。"],[92.99,99.12,65,"We trained individual models, or multi-task models without specifying the instructions.","我们要么为每个任务单独训练模型，要么做多任务训练，但不给出指令。"],[99.47,105.0,65,"So these models find it very hard to generalize to new tasks zero-shot.","所以这些模型很难零样本泛化到新任务上。"],[105.35,114.52,65,"Instruction tuning fixes this: write the instruction into the input, like, translate this into Chinese, and train on many tasks.","指令微调解决了这个问题：把指令写进输入，比如“把这句话翻译成中文”，并在大量任务上训练。"],[115.77,122.1,66,"After ChatGPT showed the power of instruction following, the open-source community moved fast.","ChatGPT 展示了指令遵循的威力之后，开源社区迅速跟进。"],[122.45,126.75,66,"It started with LLaMA, a strong open base model from Meta.","起点是 LLaMA，Meta 发布的一个强大的开源基座模型。"],[127.1,134.58,66,"Then came the instruction-tuned versions: Alpaca, Vicuna, GPT4-Alpaca, and Tulu.","接着出现了各种指令微调版本：Alpaca、Vicuna、GPT4-Alpaca 和 Tulu。"],[134.93,139.68,66,"Yes, lots of llamas, alpacas and camels!","没错，一大堆羊驼和骆驼！"],[140.03,149.46,66,"But look at the GPT-4 box on the right: multimodal input with images, and nothing there yet from the open-source world.","但看右边 GPT-4 这一栏：支持图像的多模态输入，而开源世界在这里还是一片空白。"],[150.71,154.97,67,"So where did their instruction data come from? Look at this table.","那么它们的指令数据是从哪里来的？看这张表。"],[155.32,158.52,67,"LLaMA itself has no instruction-following data.","LLaMA 本身没有指令遵循数据。"],[158.87,166.1,67,"Alpaca used GPT-3.5 as a teacher to generate fifty-two thousand examples.","Alpaca 用 GPT-3.5 做老师，生成了五万两千条数据。"],[166.45,177.14,67,"Vicuna used ShareGPT, real conversations between humans and GPT: about five hundred thousand turns from around one hundred fifty thousand conversations.","Vicuna 用的是 ShareGPT，也就是人类与 GPT 的真实对话：大约十五万段对话、五十万轮。"],[177.49,184.47,67,"GPT4-Alpaca used text-only GPT-4 as the teacher, again with fifty-two thousand examples.","GPT4-Alpaca 用纯文本的 GPT-4 做老师，同样是五万两千条。"],[184.82,188.03,67,"And Tulu mixed many data sources together.","而 Tulu 则把多种数据来源混合在一起。"],[188.38,194.07,67,"The lesson: self-instruct with a strong teacher LLM, plus mixed human data.","经验总结：用强大的教师大模型做自我指令生成，再加上混合的人类数据。"],[195.32,198.2,68,"Now here's the problem for multimodal models.","那么问题来了，多模态模型怎么办？"],[198.55,203.58,68,"For text, we could always ask a strong teacher LLM to write instruction data.","对文本来说，我们总可以请一个强大的教师大模型来写指令数据。"],[203.93,208.92,68,"But for images, there was no multimodal teacher available to generate this data.","但对图像来说，当时并没有可用的多模态老师来生成这种数据。"],[209.27,213.29,68,"This is where LLaVA, Visual Instruction Tuning, comes in.","这时 LLaVA，也就是视觉指令微调，登场了。"],[213.64,218.51,68,"The clever trick: they still used text-only GPT-4 as the teacher!","巧妙之处在于：他们用的老师依然是纯文本的 GPT-4！"],[218.86,228.0,68,"With it, they built one hundred fifty-eight thousand multimodal instruction-following samples, the first of their kind, and high quality.","借助它，他们构建了十五万八千条多模态指令遵循数据，这是首创，而且质量很高。"],[228.35,231.6,68,"Train on it, and you get a multimodal chatbot.","用它来训练，就得到了一个多模态聊天机器人。"],[231.95,236.86,68,"But wait. How can a text-only model write about images it cannot see?","等一下。一个纯文本模型，怎么能描述它根本看不见的图像呢？"],[238.11,244.16,69,"Here's the answer: describe the image in text, and let GPT-4 read that.","答案是：用文字来描述图像，然后让 GPT-4 去读这些文字。"],[244.51,249.47,69,"First, we give it rich symbolic representations of the image.","第一，给它提供图像的丰富符号化表示。"],[249.82,254.73,69,"Context type one: captions, several sentences describing the scene.","第一类上下文：描述，也就是几句描述场景的话。"],[255.08,261.7,69,"Context type two: bounding boxes, each object with its category and its coordinates.","第二类上下文：边界框，每个物体都带有类别和坐标。"],[262.05,269.12,69,"From these alone, GPT-4 knows there are people, luggage, and a vehicle in an underground parking area.","仅凭这些，GPT-4 就知道地下停车场里有人、有行李，还有一辆车。"],[269.47,277.19,69,"Second, in-context learning: we show GPT-4 a few manually written examples, so it knows what to produce.","第二，上下文学习：给 GPT-4 看几个人工写好的示例，让它知道该生成什么。"],[277.54,285.42,69,"Then text-only GPT-4 generates conversations, detailed descriptions, and complex reasoning questions about the image.","然后，纯文本的 GPT-4 就能围绕这张图生成对话、详细描述和复杂推理问题。"],[285.77,290.08,69,"Cheap, scalable, and surprisingly effective.","便宜、可扩展，而且效果出奇地好。"],[291.33,293.83,70,"Now let's put the whole framework together.","现在我们把整个框架串起来。"],[294.18,296.57,70,"On the left is data construction.","左边是数据构建。"],[296.92,303.94,70,"We can adapt existing datasets, use self-instruction with a strong teacher, and mix different data sources.","我们可以改造已有数据集，用强大的老师做自我指令生成，再把不同来源的数据混合起来。"],[304.29,309.98,70,"The result is visual instruction-following data: an image, a question, and an answer.","得到的就是视觉指令遵循数据：一张图、一个问题、一个回答。"],[310.33,318.62,70,"For example: describe the image concisely. Answer: a calico cat lying on the table, wearing black sunglasses.","比如：简洁地描述这张图。回答：一只三花猫躺在桌上，戴着一副黑色墨镜。"],[318.97,325.23,70,"On the right is the model, with LLaVA-1.5 as the example.","右边是模型，以 LLaVA-1.5 为例。"],[325.58,331.63,70,"A CLIP ViT-L vision encoder, at three hundred thirty-six pixels, encodes the image.","一个 336 像素的 CLIP ViT-L 视觉编码器对图像进行编码。"],[331.98,340.3,70,"An MLP connector maps the visual features into the language model, Vicuna version one point five, with thirteen billion parameters.","一个 MLP 连接器把视觉特征映射进语言模型，也就是一百三十亿参数的 Vicuna v1.5。"],[340.65,345.24,70,"And the user's question goes through the normal tokenizer and embedding.","用户的问题则走普通的分词器和词嵌入。"],[345.59,352.25,70,"But do we train all of this in one go? Not quite. Next, let's look at multi-stage training.","但是，这些是一次性训练完的吗？并不是。接下来我们看多阶段训练。"],[353.5,359.19,71,"Now let's put all the pieces together: multi-stage training of multimodal LLMs.","现在我们把所有部分拼起来：多模态大模型的多阶段训练。"],[359.54,368.72,71,"Why not just train everything at once? Because a vision encoder and a language model start out as strangers, and we have to introduce them step by step.","为什么不一次性把所有东西都训练好？因为视觉编码器和语言模型一开始互不相识，我们得一步一步地让它们认识彼此。"],[369.07,374.46,71,"Let's see what data each stage uses, and which parts of the model we freeze or train.","我们来看看每个阶段用什么数据，以及模型的哪些部分冻结、哪些部分训练。"],[375.71,379.28,72,"First, the training data. There are two main kinds.","首先是训练数据。主要有两类。"],[379.63,384.13,72,"The first kind is image-text paired data, basically captions.","第一类是图文配对数据，基本上就是图像描述。"],[384.48,389.4,72,"The second kind is visual instruction tuning data, like visual question answering.","第二类是视觉指令微调数据，比如视觉问答。"],[389.75,397.47,72,"So how do we get a lot of high-quality data of both kinds? This figure comes from ALLaVA, a work from our own group.","那么，怎样才能获得大量高质量的这两类数据？这张图来自 ALLaVA，是我们自己课题组的工作。"],[397.82,402.37,72,"The idea is simple: we let GPT-4V do the hard work.","思路很简单：让 GPT-4V 来干这份苦活。"],[402.72,411.69,72,"For images from LAION, GPT-4V writes a detailed caption, then a complex instruction, and then a detailed answer to that instruction.","对于来自 LAION 的图像，GPT-4V 先写一段详细描述，再生成一个复杂指令，并给出这个指令的详细回答。"],[412.04,418.63,72,"For Vision-FLAN, it writes a detailed caption and a detailed answer to the existing task instruction.","对于 Vision-FLAN，它为已有的任务指令写出详细描述和详细回答。"],[418.98,424.83,72,"One strong teacher model synthesizes both kinds of data, to train a lite vision-language model.","一个强大的教师模型同时合成这两类数据，用来训练一个轻量级的视觉语言模型。"],[426.08,430.38,73,"Let's zoom into caption data, which we use for pretraining alignment.","我们先放大看看图像描述数据，它用于预训练对齐。"],[430.73,435.24,73,"Look at this photo of a train station, and three different captions for it.","看这张火车站的照片，以及它的三种不同描述。"],[435.59,440.37,73,"The COCO captions are short, one line each: children waiting for a train.","COCO 的描述很短，每条只有一句：孩子们在等火车。"],[440.72,444.79,73,"The LLaVA caption is longer, but still fairly general.","LLaVA 的描述更长一些，但仍然比较笼统。"],[445.14,454.31,73,"The ShareGPT4V caption is much richer: the green train, the Platform 2 sign, the red signal, even the text on the warning signs.","ShareGPT4V 的描述则丰富得多：绿色的火车、二号站台的牌子、红色信号灯，甚至警示牌上的文字。"],[454.66,460.38,73,"So the first ones are called coarse-grained image-text, and the last one is fine-grained image-text.","所以前面这些叫粗粒度图文数据，最后这个叫细粒度图文数据。"],[460.73,465.44,73,"Richer captions teach the model to notice the details, not just the gist.","更丰富的描述能教会模型关注细节，而不只是大意。"],[466.69,469.7,74,"Here is the landscape of caption datasets.","这是图像描述数据集的全景。"],[470.05,474.15,74,"Coarse-grained data is huge, but the captions are short and noisy.","粗粒度数据量巨大，但描述又短又嘈杂。"],[474.5,479.46,74,"Look at LAION-5B: five point nine billion image-text pairs!","看 LAION-5B：五十九亿个图文对！"],[479.81,487.89,74,"Fine-grained data is the opposite: high quality, longer and more accurate descriptions, and finer alignment between modalities.","细粒度数据正好相反：质量高、描述更长更准确，模态之间的对齐也更精细。"],[488.24,496.07,74,"ShareGPT4V-PT has one point two million samples, and our ALLaVA has seven hundred and nine thousand.","ShareGPT4V-PT 有一百二十万条样本，我们的 ALLaVA 有七十万九千条。"],[496.42,504.02,74,"And caption data is not only about images: there is video-text, audio-text, and even chart-text data.","而且描述数据不只针对图像：还有视频-文本、音频-文本，甚至图表-文本数据。"],[504.37,509.2,74,"Both matter: coarse data gives you scale, fine data gives you precision.","两者都很重要：粗粒度数据带来规模，细粒度数据带来精度。"],[510.45,515.68,75,"Next, instruction tuning data, mostly in the form of visual question answering.","接下来是指令微调数据，主要是视觉问答的形式。"],[516.03,524.97,75,"LLaVA-Instruct-158k is the classic one: one hundred fifty-eight thousand samples, generated by ChatGPT.","LLaVA-Instruct-158k 是最经典的：十五万八千条样本，由 ChatGPT 生成。"],[525.32,536.12,75,"Now look at the Constructions column: almost every dataset is generated by a strong model, like ChatGPT, GPT-4, or GPT-3.5-turbo.","再看“构建方式”这一列：几乎每个数据集都是由强大的模型生成的，比如 ChatGPT、GPT-4 或 GPT-3.5-turbo。"],[536.47,542.84,75,"And the modalities go beyond images: charts, audio, video, and even point clouds.","而且模态也超出了图像：有图表、音频、视频，甚至点云。"],[543.19,548.11,75,"MIMIC-IT is the largest one here, with two point eight million samples.","MIMIC-IT 是这里最大的，有二百八十万条样本。"],[548.46,559.33,75,"And at the bottom, ALLaVA-4V: one point three million samples, generated by GPT-4V, a model that can actually look at the image.","最下面是 ALLaVA-4V：一百三十万条样本，由 GPT-4V 生成，而它是真正能看到图像的模型。"],[559.68,566.51,75,"Here's the key idea: when human labeling is too expensive, we distill from a stronger model.","关键思想是：当人工标注太昂贵时，我们就从更强的模型中蒸馏。"],[567.76,573.89,76,"So how do we use these two kinds of data? Here is the typical two-stage training paradigm.","那么，这两类数据怎么用？这就是典型的两阶段训练范式。"],[574.24,580.45,76,"Stage one is pretraining: its goal is to align different modalities and provide world knowledge.","第一阶段是预训练：目标是对齐不同模态，并提供世界知识。"],[580.8,587.87,76,"Look at the fire icon: only the adapter is trained, while the vision encoder and the large language model stay frozen.","看这个火焰图标：只有适配器在训练，视觉编码器和大语言模型都保持冻结。"],[588.22,596.38,76,"The adapter learns to map image features into the word embedding space of the LLM, using simple image-caption pairs.","适配器利用简单的图文描述对，学习把图像特征映射到大模型的词嵌入空间中。"],[596.73,604.94,76,"Stage two is instruction tuning: it teaches the model to understand instructions from users and fulfill the demanded tasks.","第二阶段是指令微调：教模型理解用户的指令，并完成所要求的任务。"],[605.29,612.32,76,"Now the fire is on the large language model too, so both the adapter and the LLM are updated.","现在火焰也烧到了大语言模型上，所以适配器和大模型都会被更新。"],[612.67,619.9,76,"Why two stages? First, connect the eyes to the brain cheaply; then, teach the whole system to follow instructions.","为什么要分两阶段？先用很低的成本把“眼睛”接到“大脑”上，再教整个系统听从指令。"],[621.15,626.92,77,"Of course, different models make different choices. Let's compare four popular ones.","当然，不同的模型会做出不同的选择。我们来比较四个流行的模型。"],[627.27,636.33,77,"The legend: a snowflake means frozen, a fire means trainable, and the icons below mark text data versus multimodal data.","图例：雪花表示冻结，火焰表示可训练，下面的图标区分纯文本数据和多模态数据。"],[636.68,645.9,77,"MiniGPT-4 keeps both the LLM and the visual encoder frozen in both stages; only the connection between them is trained.","MiniGPT-4 在两个阶段都冻结大模型和视觉编码器，只训练两者之间的连接部分。"],[646.25,654.6,77,"Kosmos-1 trains the LLM already in stage one, and its stage two uses text-only instruction data.","Kosmos-1 在第一阶段就训练大模型，而它的第二阶段只用纯文本指令数据。"],[654.95,662.3,77,"LLaVA is the typical recipe we just saw: freeze both in stage one, then unfreeze the LLM in stage two.","LLaVA 就是我们刚才看到的典型配方：第一阶段两者都冻结，第二阶段解冻大模型。"],[662.65,672.16,77,"mPLUG-Owl does something different: it trains the visual encoder in stage one, then tunes the LLM with both multimodal and text data.","mPLUG-Owl 的做法不同：第一阶段训练视觉编码器，第二阶段用多模态和纯文本数据一起微调大模型。"],[672.51,681.73,77,"Notice the common pattern: stage one always uses image-text data, and whenever the LLM is trained, the visual encoder is frozen.","注意其中的共同规律：第一阶段都使用图文数据，而且只要大模型在训练，视觉编码器就是冻结的。"],[682.98,688.51,78,"Let me bring us back to the big picture, and highlight stage one, the pretraining stage.","我们回到整体框架，重点看第一阶段，也就是预训练阶段。"],[688.86,694.29,78,"Its job is to align the modalities and provide world knowledge, through the trainable adapter.","它的任务是通过可训练的适配器，对齐各个模态并提供世界知识。"],[694.64,702.12,78,"This stage is cheap, because the big LLM stays frozen, but it builds the bridge that everything later depends on.","这个阶段成本很低，因为庞大的语言模型是冻结的，但它搭起了后续一切都依赖的桥梁。"],[702.47,707.83,78,"Then stage two unlocks the LLM, so the model learns to follow instructions.","然后第二阶段解冻大模型，让模型学会遵循指令。"],[708.18,716.1,78,"Pretraining to align, instruction tuning to follow: that is the core recipe behind most multimodal LLMs today.","预训练负责对齐，指令微调负责听话：这就是如今大多数多模态大模型背后的核心配方。"],[716.45,721.77,78,"So far, our models can see. Next, let's teach them to hear and speak!","到目前为止，我们的模型已经能“看”了。接下来，我们教它们去听、去说！"]]},{"n":5,"title":"Speech Language Models","blurb":"Self-supervised units and neural codecs, interleaving speech with text, full-duplex dialogue and omni models.","file":"lecture10_part5.mp4","poster":"lecture10_part5.jpg","duration":969.9,"first":79,"last":94,"slides":[{"n":79,"title":"5 Speech Language Models","t":0.8},{"n":80,"title":"Why Speech Is Hard for Language Models","t":21.99},{"n":81,"title":"An Interesting Question: Speech Without Words?","t":93.69},{"n":82,"title":"An Interesting Question: A Speech-to-Speech Stress Test","t":141.58},{"n":83,"title":"Cascade vs. End-to-End Spoken Dialogue","t":192.74},{"n":84,"title":"Semantic Tokens: Self-Supervised Units (HuBERT, wav2vec 2.0)","t":255.99},{"n":85,"title":"Acoustic Tokens: Neural Codecs and Residual Vector Quantization","t":334.24},{"n":86,"title":"Semantic vs. Acoustic Tokens — and Hybrid Tokenizers","t":404.85},{"n":87,"title":"Speech Tokenizers at a Glance","t":486.21},{"n":88,"title":"Teaching an LLM to Speak: Interleaving Text and Speech","t":556.15},{"n":89,"title":"Full-Duplex Dialogue: Listening While Speaking (Moshi)","t":616.3},{"n":90,"title":"Seeduplex: Full-Duplex Voice Interaction (ByteDance Seed)","t":683.87},{"n":91,"title":"Omni Models: The Thinker–Talker Architecture","t":718.77},{"n":92,"title":"End-to-End Speech LLMs: The 2024–2025 Landscape","t":801.12},{"n":93,"title":"Our Take: What Omni Models Must Do Differently","t":848.29},{"n":94,"title":"Voice Will Be the Ultimate Interface","t":919.13}],"sents":[[0.8,3.48,79,"Part five: Speech Language Models!","第五部分：语音语言模型！"],[3.83,12.32,79,"Speech is the most natural interface we have, but it is continuous, fast, and full of information that is not in the text.","语音是我们最自然的交互方式，但它是连续的、快速的，而且充满了文字之外的信息。"],[12.67,20.59,79,"So how do we turn sound into tokens that an LLM can model? That is the question for this whole part.","那么，怎样把声音变成大模型能够建模的 token？这就是整个这一部分要回答的问题。"],[21.84,26.79,80,"First, why is speech so hard for a language model? There are four reasons.","首先，为什么语音对语言模型来说这么难？有四个原因。"],[27.14,36.17,80,"One, it is continuous: a waveform has sixteen to twenty-four thousand samples per second, and there are no natural words to tokenize.","第一，它是连续的：波形每秒有一万六到两万四千个采样点，也没有天然的“词”可以切分。"],[36.52,46.47,80,"Two, it is long: one second of speech is only two or three words of text, but fifty to seventy-five frames of a typical encoder.","第二，它很长：一秒语音只对应两三个文字词，却对应典型编码器的五十到七十五帧。"],[46.82,54.77,80,"Three, it is rich: beyond the words, there is speaker identity, emotion, prosody, laughter, and background sound.","第三，它很丰富：除了文字内容，还有说话人身份、情绪、韵律、笑声和背景声音。"],[55.12,63.93,80,"And four, it is real-time: a conversation needs replies within about two to three hundred milliseconds, with overlaps and interruptions.","第四，它要求实时：对话需要在大约两三百毫秒内回应，还会有重叠和打断。"],[64.28,69.68,80,"So here is the central design question: what exactly is a speech token?","所以，核心的设计问题是：语音 token 究竟是什么？"],[70.03,75.46,80,"It decides what the model can hear, what it can say, and how fast.","它决定了模型能听到什么、能说出什么，以及速度有多快。"],[75.81,83.32,80,"Look at the numbers: text is about three to four tokens per second of speech, and HuBERT units are fifty per second.","看这些数字：每秒语音对应的文本大约三到四个 token，而 HuBERT 单元是每秒五十个。"],[83.67,92.29,80,"And EnCodec has seventy-five frames per second, each with up to thirty-two codebooks. That is a huge gap in sequence length!","而 EnCodec 每秒有七十五帧，每帧最多三十二个码本。序列长度的差距非常大！"],[93.54,98.45,81,"Before we look at tokenizers, here's an interesting question to think about.","在看具体的 tokenizer 之前，先来思考一个有趣的问题。"],[98.8,103.83,81,"Can speech-to-speech models work in general without involving language, without words at all?","语音到语音的模型，能不能在完全不涉及语言、不涉及文字的情况下工作？"],[104.18,112.75,81,"On the left is the classic cascade: an ASR model transcribes the speech, and the LLM reads the transcription.","左边是经典的级联方式：ASR 模型把语音转写成文字，大模型再读取转写结果。"],[113.1,120.69,81,"Notice the dashed line: non-semantic information, like emotion and stress, gets cut off at the transcription.","注意这条虚线：情绪、重音这类非语义信息，在转写这一步就被截断了。"],[121.04,129.57,81,"On the right, a speech LLM feeds the acoustic encoder's output directly into the LLM, so those cues can be kept.","右边的语音大模型把声学编码器的输出直接送进大模型，所以这些线索可以被保留下来。"],[129.92,137.84,81,"Sounds great, right? But some people argue: without language, the model probably cannot really think, reason, or plan.","听起来很棒，对吧？但也有人认为：没有语言，模型可能就无法真正地思考、推理和规划。"],[138.19,140.18,81,"Let me show you a concrete test.","我给大家看一个具体的测试。"],[141.43,144.27,82,"Here is a speech-to-speech stress test.","这是一个语音到语音的压力测试。"],[144.62,150.31,82,"Ask the model: count from one to one hundred, pausing whenever you encounter a prime number.","让模型：从一数到一百，每遇到一个质数就停顿一下。"],[150.66,161.79,82,"The correct output goes like this: one, two, pause, three, pause, four, five, pause, and so on, all the way to one hundred.","正确的输出是这样的：一，二，停顿，三，停顿，四，五，停顿……一直数到一百。"],[162.14,168.97,82,"To do this, the model must decide for every single number whether it is prime, right before it speaks it.","要做到这一点，模型必须在说出每个数之前，判断它是不是质数。"],[169.32,177.73,82,"With text, a model can first write out its reasoning step by step; a pure speech model has no such scratchpad.","如果有文字，模型可以先一步步写出推理过程；而纯语音模型没有这样的草稿纸。"],[178.08,183.88,82,"So the claim here is: without textual planning, speech-to-speech might not solve this problem.","所以这里的观点是：没有文本层面的规划，语音到语音模型可能解决不了这个问题。"],[184.23,191.34,82,"Keep this in mind; it helps explain why many speech models still produce text alongside the speech.","请记住这一点，它有助于解释为什么许多语音模型仍然会在生成语音的同时生成文字。"],[192.59,196.56,83,"Now let's compare two ways to build a spoken dialogue system.","现在我们来比较构建语音对话系统的两种方式。"],[196.91,207.43,83,"The cascade approach, around two thousand twenty-three, chains three models: ASR like Whisper, then an LLM, then text-to-speech.","级联方式大约在二〇二三年流行，它串联三个模型：像 Whisper 这样的 ASR，然后是大模型，最后是语音合成。"],[207.78,211.06,83,"It works, but it has three problems.","它能用，但有三个问题。"],[211.41,219.57,83,"It loses emotion and speaker cues at the text bottleneck, the latency adds up to one to three seconds, and turn-taking is strict.","在文本这个瓶颈处会丢失情绪和说话人线索，延迟累加起来达到一到三秒，而且轮流发言非常死板。"],[219.92,228.33,83,"The end-to-end approach, from two thousand twenty-four on, uses one model that hears and speaks tokens directly.","端到端方式从二〇二四年开始兴起，用一个模型直接听和说 token。"],[228.68,236.16,83,"Speech goes through a speech tokenizer, into a speech-text language model, and out through a speech decoder.","语音先经过语音 tokenizer，进入语音-文本语言模型，再通过语音解码器输出。"],[236.51,247.56,83,"This keeps the paralinguistic information, streams with about two hundred milliseconds latency, and can even listen while speaking, which we call full duplex.","这样能保留副语言信息，以大约两百毫秒的延迟流式输出，甚至可以边说边听，也就是全双工。"],[247.91,252.66,83,"And notice: everything now hinges on the tokenizer in the middle.","注意：现在一切都取决于中间的这个 tokenizer。"],[253.01,254.59,83,"So let's open that box.","那我们就把这个盒子打开看看。"],[255.84,261.97,84,"The first family is semantic tokens, from self-supervised models like HuBERT and wav2vec 2.0.","第一类是语义 token，来自 HuBERT 和 wav2vec 2.0 这类自监督模型。"],[262.32,271.29,84,"Here is the pipeline: the waveform goes through a CNN encoder, then a Transformer trained with masked prediction.","流程是这样的：波形先经过 CNN 编码器，再经过一个用掩码预测训练的 Transformer。"],[271.64,280.74,84,"This gives features at fifty per second, and k-means turns each frame into a cluster ID, with K from one hundred to two thousand.","这样得到每秒五十个特征，再用 k-means 把每一帧变成一个聚类编号，K 在一百到两千之间。"],[281.09,288.44,84,"So speech becomes a sequence of discrete units: seventy-one, seventy-one, twelve, twelve, twelve, and so on.","于是语音变成了一串离散单元：七十一、七十一、十二、十二、十二，等等。"],[288.79,298.34,84,"Merge the repeats, and we get seventy-one, twelve, eighty-eight, five, forty, which looks a lot like text!","把重复的合并，就得到七十一、十二、八十八、五、四十，看起来很像文本！"],[298.69,307.66,84,"How does HuBERT learn? It masks spans of audio and predicts the cluster IDs of the masked frames, just like BERT's masked language model.","HuBERT 怎么学习？它遮住一段段音频，去预测被遮住帧的聚类编号，就像 BERT 的掩码语言模型。"],[308.01,315.69,84,"The targets first come from k-means on MFCCs, and then from its own features, and the process iterates.","预测目标一开始来自对 MFCC 的 k-means 聚类，之后来自模型自身的特征，如此迭代。"],[316.04,324.33,84,"What do the units keep? Phonetic content, which is friendly for language models and enables textless NLP, like GSLM.","这些单元保留了什么？音素内容，它对语言模型很友好，也让 GSLM 这样的“无文本 NLP”成为可能。"],[324.68,332.84,84,"What do they lose? Speaker, emotion and fine prosody are mostly gone, so you need a vocoder like unit-HiFi-GAN to speak.","丢失了什么？说话人、情绪和细腻的韵律基本都没了，所以要发声还需要 unit-HiFi-GAN 这样的声码器。"],[334.09,338.23,85,"The second family is acoustic tokens, from neural codecs.","第二类是声学 token，来自神经音频编解码器。"],[338.58,345.93,85,"A codec encodes the waveform, quantizes it, and then decodes it back into a waveform.","编解码器先编码波形，再量化，最后解码回波形。"],[346.28,348.87,85,"The trick is residual vector quantization.","其中的关键技巧是残差向量量化。"],[349.22,357.22,85,"The first codebook captures a coarse version; each next stage quantizes the residual, the error left by the previous one.","第一个码本捕捉一个粗略版本；之后每一级都量化上一级留下的残差，也就是剩余误差。"],[357.57,365.97,85,"This illustrative chart shows the idea: each extra codebook removes part of the remaining error, so the error shrinks quickly.","这张示意图说明了这个思路：每多一个码本就消除一部分剩余误差，所以误差下降得很快。"],[366.32,373.06,85,"The bitrate is the frame rate, times the number of codebooks, times the bits per code.","码率等于帧率乘以码本数量，再乘以每个码的比特数。"],[373.41,378.97,85,"SoundStream was the first RVQ codec, at three to eighteen kilobits per second.","SoundStream 是第一个 RVQ 编解码器，码率为每秒三到十八千比特。"],[379.32,387.16,85,"EnCodec runs at seventy-five hertz with two to thirty-two codebooks, giving one point five to twenty-four kilobits per second.","EnCodec 的帧率是七十五赫兹，使用二到三十二个码本，码率为每秒一点五到二十四千比特。"],[387.51,395.87,85,"And Mimi: twelve point five hertz, times eight codebooks, times eleven bits, which is only one point one kilobits per second!","再看 Mimi：十二点五赫兹，乘以八个码本，再乘以十一比特，只有每秒一点一千比特！"],[396.22,403.45,85,"And a nice property: drop the late codebooks, and you get a lower bitrate with worse quality, like a quality dial.","还有一个很好的性质：去掉后面的码本，码率降低、音质变差，就像一个音质旋钮。"],[404.7,408.63,86,"So now we have two kinds of tokens. Let's compare them.","现在我们有了两类 token。来比较一下。"],[408.98,418.74,86,"Semantic tokens capture the content and are easy for an LM to model over long ranges, but they lose voice and emotion, and need a vocoder.","语义 token 捕捉内容，语言模型容易建模长程依赖，但它们丢失了音色和情绪，还需要声码器。"],[419.09,425.59,86,"Acoustic tokens reconstruct the exact voice and sound, but there are many of them, so long-range modeling is hard.","声学 token 能精确还原声音和音色，但数量很多，所以长程建模很困难。"],[425.94,432.6,86,"Can we get the best of both? AudioLM, from two thousand twenty-two, generates in a hierarchy.","能不能两者兼得？二〇二二年的 AudioLM 采用分层生成。"],[432.95,442.17,86,"First semantic tokens for what is said, then coarse acoustic tokens for who and how, then fine acoustic tokens for the details.","先生成语义 token，决定说什么；再生成粗粒度声学 token，决定谁在说、怎么说；最后生成细粒度声学 token，补充细节。"],[442.52,448.98,86,"Another idea is a hybrid tokenizer: one codec, whose first codebook is semantic.","另一种思路是混合 tokenizer：只用一个编解码器，但它的第一个码本是语义的。"],[449.33,459.11,86,"SpeechTokenizer uses eight-level RVQ at fifty hertz; level one is distilled from HuBERT for content, and levels two to eight carry timbre and details.","SpeechTokenizer 使用五十赫兹的八级 RVQ；第一级从 HuBERT 蒸馏而来，负责内容，第二到第八级负责音色和细节。"],[459.46,471.41,86,"Mimi, from Kyutai, is streaming at twelve point five hertz: one semantic codebook distilled from WavLM, plus seven acoustic RVQ levels, with eighty millisecond frames.","Kyutai 的 Mimi 以十二点五赫兹流式运行：一个从 WavLM 蒸馏的语义码本，加上七级声学 RVQ，每帧八十毫秒。"],[471.76,478.87,86,"Content first, then the voice: one token stream that a language model can both understand and speak.","先内容，后声音：一条语言模型既能理解、又能说出来的 token 流。"],[479.22,484.81,86,"Before we see how a language model uses these tokens, let's compare them all at a glance.","在看语言模型如何使用这些 token 之前，我们先把它们放在一起比较一下。"],[486.06,488.24,87,"Here they are, side by side.","它们都在这里，放在一起对比。"],[488.59,496.55,87,"Look at the columns: frame rate, number of codebooks, bitrate, and the type of information each token carries.","看这几列：帧率、码本数量、比特率，以及每个 token 携带的信息类型。"],[496.9,506.24,87,"HuBERT units are purely semantic: fifty tokens per second, one codebook, only about zero point four five kilobits per second.","HuBERT 单元是纯语义的：每秒 50 个 token，一个码本，只有大约 0.45 kbps。"],[506.59,515.24,87,"SoundStream and EnCodec are acoustic codecs: seventy-five hertz, with residual vector quantization stacking many codebooks.","SoundStream 和 EnCodec 是声学编解码器：75 赫兹，用残差向量量化叠加许多码本。"],[515.59,524.36,87,"SpeechTokenizer is a hybrid: its first codebook level is distilled from HuBERT, so it carries meaning, and the rest carry acoustics.","SpeechTokenizer 是混合型的：第一层码本从 HuBERT 蒸馏而来，承载语义，其余层承载声学细节。"],[524.71,533.47,87,"Then in two thousand twenty-four, Mimi and the GLM-4-Voice tokenizer drop all the way down to twelve point five hertz.","到了 2024 年，Mimi 和 GLM-4-Voice tokenizer 一路降到了 12.5 赫兹。"],[533.82,540.77,87,"Here's the key trend: fewer tokens per second, getting closer to text, which runs at only three to four tokens per second.","关键趋势是：每秒 token 越来越少，越来越接近文本——文本每秒只有三到四个 token。"],[541.12,548.87,87,"Why does that matter? Because then the language model spends its capacity on meaning, not on raw audio samples.","为什么这很重要？因为这样语言模型就能把能力花在语义上，而不是原始音频采样上。"],[549.22,554.75,87,"Okay, so we have speech tokens. How do we teach an LLM to actually speak with them?","好，我们有了语音 token。那怎么教一个 LLM 用它们真正开口说话呢？"],[556.0,559.53,88,"Here are three recipes, from simple to clever.","这里有三种方法，从简单到巧妙。"],[559.88,568.41,88,"Recipe one: extend the vocabulary. Add speech tokens to a text LLM and continue pre-training on speech.","第一种：扩展词表。把语音 token 加进文本 LLM，然后在语音上继续预训练。"],[568.76,574.48,88,"But be careful: the model keeps its text knowledge only if text data stays in the training mix.","但要小心：只有训练数据里一直保留文本，模型才能保住它的文本知识。"],[574.83,583.4,88,"Recipe two: interleave at the word level. Look at this example: the cat, then a few speech tokens, then on the mat.","第二种：在词级别交错。看这个例子：the cat，然后是几个语音 token，再接 on the mat。"],[583.75,591.43,88,"SpiritLM switches modality in the middle of a sentence, and that helps knowledge transfer from text to speech.","SpiritLM 在句子中间切换模态，这有助于知识从文本迁移到语音。"],[591.78,600.23,88,"Recipe three: think in text, speak in speech. The text tokens run slightly ahead of the speech tokens they produce.","第三种：用文本思考，用语音说话。文本 token 会略微领先于它们生成的语音 token。"],[600.58,607.52,88,"GLM-4-Voice alternates text and speech chunks, and Moshi calls this its inner monologue.","GLM-4-Voice 交替生成文本块和语音块，Moshi 则把这叫作它的“内心独白”。"],[607.87,614.9,88,"So here's the lesson: text is the LLM's strongest modality, so use it as a scaffold, don't throw it away.","所以结论是：文本是 LLM 最强的模态，要把它当作脚手架，而不是丢掉它。"],[616.15,619.84,89,"Now, real conversation is not like a walkie-talkie.","现在，真实的对话可不像对讲机。"],[620.19,627.83,89,"Most voice assistants are half duplex: the user speaks, the model waits, then the model speaks. We take turns.","大多数语音助手是半双工的：用户说完，模型等待，然后模型再说。大家轮流来。"],[628.18,635.98,89,"But humans do something richer. We say mm-hm while the other person is talking, we interrupt, we overlap.","但人类做的事情丰富得多。别人说话时我们会说“嗯嗯”，会打断，会重叠着说。"],[636.33,642.75,89,"Full duplex means modeling both streams at once: the model is listening while it is speaking.","全双工意味着同时建模两条流：模型一边说，一边在听。"],[643.1,648.5,89,"Moshi does this with Mimi tokens at twelve point five hertz, for both speakers.","Moshi 的做法是：对双方说话人都使用 12.5 赫兹的 Mimi token。"],[648.85,658.83,89,"It uses an inner monologue of time-aligned text tokens, plus an RQ-Transformer: a big temporal model and a small depth model over codebooks.","它使用由时间对齐文本 token 构成的内心独白，再加上 RQ-Transformer：一个大的时间模型和一个小的码本深度模型。"],[659.18,665.56,89,"And the latency? One hundred sixty milliseconds in theory, about two hundred in practice.","延迟呢？理论上 160 毫秒，实际大约 200 毫秒。"],[665.91,673.95,89,"That is within the natural gap between human turns, about two hundred to three hundred milliseconds. It feels like a real person!","这在人类自然换话的间隔之内，大约 200 到 300 毫秒。感觉就像在和真人说话！"],[674.3,682.47,89,"And since then, Seeduplex, MiniCPM-o and DuplexOmni have brought full duplex to omni models.","此后，Seeduplex、MiniCPM-o 和 DuplexOmni 把全双工带进了全模态模型。"],[683.72,690.17,90,"Here is what full duplex looks like in a real product: Seeduplex from ByteDance Seed.","这是全双工在真实产品中的样子：字节跳动 Seed 的 Seeduplex。"],[690.52,698.0,90,"An elderly man is talking to the assistant on his phone, and he pauses: let me think.","一位老人正在用手机和助手对话，他停了下来：让我想一下。"],[698.35,704.56,90,"A naive system might jump in right away, because it hears silence and assumes he is done.","一个简单的系统可能会立刻插话，因为它听到了沉默，就以为他说完了。"],[704.91,712.39,90,"But here, the caption says he is trying to recall forgotten lyrics, and the model waits patiently.","但在这里，字幕说他正在回忆忘掉的歌词，而模型耐心地等待。"],[712.74,717.37,90,"Knowing when not to speak is just as important as knowing what to say.","知道什么时候不该说话，和知道该说什么一样重要。"],[718.62,723.58,91,"Now let's go beyond speech, to omni models that take everything in.","现在我们超越语音，来看能接收一切输入的全模态模型。"],[723.93,734.93,91,"Text, image, audio and video all flow into one big model called the Thinker, an LLM, often a mixture of experts.","文本、图像、音频和视频都流入一个叫作 Thinker 的大模型，它是一个 LLM，通常是混合专家模型。"],[735.28,738.81,91,"The Thinker can directly write a text answer.","Thinker 可以直接写出文本回答。"],[739.16,746.39,91,"But it also passes its hidden states to a second model, the Talker, which produces speech tokens.","它还会把隐藏状态传给第二个模型 Talker，由 Talker 生成语音 token。"],[746.74,751.7,91,"A codec decoder then turns those tokens into the actual speech you hear.","然后由编解码器的解码器把这些 token 变成你听到的真实语音。"],[752.05,760.01,91,"Why split it? The Thinker focuses on understanding and reasoning, while the Talker focuses on sounding natural and fast.","为什么要拆开？Thinker 专注于理解和推理，而 Talker 专注于说得自然、说得快。"],[760.36,771.52,91,"GPT-4o showed in two thousand twenty-four that one network can handle text, vision and audio, at about three hundred twenty milliseconds latency.","GPT-4o 在 2024 年展示了一个网络就能处理文本、视觉和音频，平均语音延迟约 320 毫秒。"],[771.87,781.38,91,"Qwen2.5-Omni introduced the Thinker-Talker split, with time-aligned positions called TMRoPE for audio and video.","Qwen2.5-Omni 引入了 Thinker-Talker 拆分，并用称为 TMRoPE 的时间对齐位置编码处理音频和视频。"],[781.73,793.11,91,"Qwen3-Omni and Qwen3.5-Omni go further: mixture-of-experts Thinker and Talker, about two hundred thirty-four milliseconds latency.","Qwen3-Omni 和 Qwen3.5-Omni 更进一步：Thinker 和 Talker 都是混合专家结构，延迟约 234 毫秒。"],[793.46,799.72,91,"They also use an RVQ audio tokenizer and a two hundred fifty-six K context window.","它们还使用 RVQ 音频 tokenizer，以及 256K 的上下文窗口。"],[800.97,806.09,92,"Let's zoom out and look at the wider landscape of end-to-end speech LLMs.","我们把视野拉远，看看端到端语音 LLM 的整体格局。"],[806.44,814.92,92,"End-to-end means speech in, speech out, without gluing together separate ASR and TTS systems.","端到端意味着语音进、语音出，而不是把独立的语音识别和语音合成系统拼接起来。"],[815.27,819.7,92,"Mini-Omni offers real-time speech interaction with streaming output.","Mini-Omni 提供带流式输出的实时语音交互。"],[820.05,826.1,92,"GLM-4-Voice from Zhipu AI targets voice conversation with emotional control.","智谱 AI 的 GLM-4-Voice 面向带情感控制的语音对话。"],[826.45,832.5,92,"Echo-X does speech-to-speech generation while preserving speaker identity and emotion.","Echo-X 做语音到语音的生成，同时保留说话人身份和情感。"],[832.85,840.73,92,"And Qwen2-Audio and Qwen2.5-Omni handle multi-turn audio understanding and generation.","而 Qwen2-Audio 和 Qwen2.5-Omni 处理多轮音频理解与生成。"],[841.08,846.89,92,"Different teams, different tricks, but the same goal: talk to the machine like you talk to a person.","不同的团队，不同的技巧，但目标相同：像和人说话一样和机器对话。"],[848.14,853.57,93,"So what have we learned? Here is our take on what omni models must do differently.","那我们学到了什么？这是我们对全模态模型必须有何不同的看法。"],[853.92,862.57,93,"One: time is the native axis. Audio and video are continuous streams, so models must be always-on and streaming, not turn-based.","第一：时间是原生的轴。音频和视频是连续的流，所以模型必须一直在线、流式处理，而不是轮流式的。"],[862.92,870.64,93,"Two: don't squeeze everything through text. Emotion, speaker identity and environment sounds must survive tokenization.","第二：不要把一切都挤过文本。情感、说话人身份和环境声音都必须在 token 化后保留下来。"],[870.99,874.08,93,"Text is a scaffold, not a bottleneck.","文本是脚手架，而不是瓶颈。"],[874.43,883.97,93,"Three: decouple thinking from talking. A slow reasoner and a fast speaker run asynchronously: think while listening, speak while thinking.","第三：把思考和说话解耦。慢的推理器和快的说话器异步运行：边听边想，边想边说。"],[884.32,893.98,93,"Four: evaluate interaction, not transcripts. Turn-taking, backchannels, interruptions and latency matter as much as word error rate.","第四：评估交互，而不是转录文本。轮换、附和、打断和延迟，和词错误率一样重要。"],[894.33,904.52,93,"Five: data is the bottleneck. Real full-duplex conversations are scarce, and synthetic TTS dialogue risks flat, uniform prosody.","第五：数据是瓶颈。真实的全双工对话很稀缺，而用语音合成造的对话容易韵律平淡、单一。"],[904.87,914.42,93,"And six: an omni model is an agent in a stream. Hearing and seeing a live world is the first step toward acting in it.","第六：全模态模型是流中的智能体。听到并看到一个实时的世界，是在其中行动的第一步。"],[914.77,917.73,93,"We will come back to that idea in Part seven.","我们会在第七部分回到这个想法。"],[918.98,924.13,94,"Let me end this part with a bold claim: voice will be the ultimate interface.","让我用一个大胆的论断来结束这一部分：语音将是终极交互界面。"],[924.48,931.02,94,"For every individual, in business products or consumer products, the ultimate user interface is voice.","对每个人来说，无论是企业产品还是消费产品，终极的用户界面都是语音。"],[931.37,935.68,94,"It is voice-driven: you speak instead of typing and tapping.","它是语音驱动的：你用说话代替打字和点击。"],[936.03,941.59,94,"It is always available, and always listening, giving ambient, proactive help.","它随时可用，而且一直在听，提供无处不在、主动的帮助。"],[941.94,946.72,94,"It has unlimited memory, remembering your context across years.","它拥有无限的记忆，能记住你多年来的上下文。"],[947.07,953.49,94,"And it becomes increasingly invisible: the device disappears, but the assistant remains.","而且它变得越来越隐形：设备消失了，助手依然在。"],[953.84,963.22,94,"Of course, there are open questions: privacy of always-on listening, trust, and when an assistant should simply stay silent.","当然，还有一些开放问题：一直在听带来的隐私问题、信任，以及助手什么时候应该保持沉默。"],[963.57,968.08,94,"Think about it: would you want an assistant that is always listening to you?","想一想：你会想要一个一直在听你说话的助手吗？"]]},{"n":6,"title":"Generation and World Simulators","blurb":"Unified understanding and generation, next-frame prediction, and video models as world simulators.","file":"lecture10_part6.mp4","poster":"lecture10_part6.jpg","duration":307.8,"first":95,"last":101,"slides":[{"n":95,"title":"6 Generation and World Simulators","t":0.8},{"n":96,"title":"Generated by Nano Banana","t":16.86},{"n":97,"title":"Janus","t":50.82},{"n":98,"title":"Large vision models using next-frame prediction","t":116.74},{"n":99,"title":"Unify multi-modal understanding and generation","t":160.28},{"n":100,"title":"Medical Sora: Towards a Medical World Simulator","t":203.5},{"n":101,"title":"Micro world simulator","t":249.07}],"sents":[[0.8,4.17,95,"Part six: generation and world simulators!","第六部分：生成与世界模拟器！"],[4.52,7.02,95,"Understanding is only half the story.","理解只是故事的一半。"],[7.37,15.46,95,"The same models increasingly generate images, videos, and even whole simulated worlds. Let's see how far this goes.","同样的模型越来越多地生成图像、视频，甚至整个模拟世界。我们来看看这能走多远。"],[16.71,21.18,96,"Let's start with a picture. This image was generated by Nano Banana.","我们从一张图开始。这张图是由 Nano Banana 生成的。"],[21.53,29.04,96,"Here is the prompt: draw a bar in a future world, like a spaceship, with robots pouring drinks and chatting.","提示词是：画一个未来世界里像宇宙飞船一样的酒吧，机器人在倒酒、聊天。"],[29.39,36.65,96,"Look at the result: a robot bartender pouring drinks with several arms, and outer space outside the window.","看看结果：一个机器人调酒师用好几只手臂倒酒，窗外是浩瀚的太空。"],[37.0,42.37,96,"And on the screens, doomsday scenes on Earth, exactly as requested.","屏幕上是地球末日的景象，完全符合要求。"],[42.72,49.42,96,"Every detail of a long, complex prompt is followed. So how do models learn to generate like this?","一个又长又复杂的提示词，每个细节都被照顾到了。那么模型是怎么学会这样生成的呢？"],[50.67,59.64,97,"One answer is to let the same LLM both understand and generate images. Janus is a model built on this idea.","一个答案是让同一个 LLM 既理解图像又生成图像。Janus 就是基于这个思路的模型。"],[59.99,72.22,97,"This figure comes from our own work, ShareGPT-4o-Image, which aligns a Janus-style model with GPT-4o-level image generation.","这张图来自我们自己的工作 ShareGPT-4o-Image，它让一个 Janus 类模型对齐到 GPT-4o 级别的图像生成能力。"],[72.57,78.74,97,"In text-to-image, a prompt like generate an oak stool photo goes in as text tokens.","在文本生成图像中，像“生成一张橡木凳子照片”这样的提示词作为文本 token 输入。"],[79.09,85.06,97,"The LLM outputs image tokens one by one, and we stitch them back into a picture.","LLM 逐个输出图像 token，然后我们把它们拼接回一张图片。"],[85.41,94.18,97,"In text-image-to-image, the input image enters twice: as embeddings from an image encoder, and as discrete image tokens.","在文本加图像生成图像中，输入图像进入两次：一次是图像编码器得到的嵌入，一次是离散的图像 token。"],[94.53,100.25,97,"Then an instruction like convert to Ghibli style produces a brand-new edited image.","然后像“转换成吉卜力风格”这样的指令，就能生成一张全新的编辑后的图像。"],[100.6,109.22,97,"Notice the training trick: parts of the input are randomly masked, ten percent of the time in one case and fifty percent in the other.","注意这里的训练技巧：部分输入会被随机遮蔽，一种情况是 10% 的概率，另一种是 50%。"],[109.57,115.34,97,"The key idea: image generation becomes next-token prediction, just like text.","核心思想是：图像生成变成了下一个 token 的预测，就和文本一样。"],[116.59,123.41,98,"Now, what if we take next-token prediction and apply it to video, with no text at all?","那么，如果把下一个 token 预测用在视频上，而且完全不用文本呢？"],[123.76,131.08,98,"That is the idea of the large vision model, LVM: predict the next frame, given previous frames as the prompt.","这就是大视觉模型 LVM 的思路：以之前的帧作为提示，预测下一帧。"],[131.43,137.2,98,"The blue boxes are the prompt frames, and the red boxes are the frames the model generated.","蓝色框里是提示帧，红色框里是模型生成的帧。"],[137.55,143.24,98,"Look at the van: as the camera moves, the model continues the motion in a plausible way.","看这辆面包车：随着镜头移动，模型以合理的方式延续了运动。"],[143.59,151.54,98,"And in these longer sequences, it predicts several future frames, considering both dynamic objects and camera motion.","在这些更长的序列中，它预测了未来的好几帧，同时考虑了动态物体和镜头运动。"],[151.89,158.88,98,"Here's why this matters: to predict the next frame well, a model must learn something about how the world moves.","这件事为什么重要：要把下一帧预测好，模型就必须学到世界是如何运动的。"],[160.13,167.27,99,"And this direction has exploded. Here is a map of unified models for multimodal understanding and generation.","这个方向已经爆发了。这是一张多模态理解与生成统一模型的全景图。"],[167.62,175.16,99,"The timeline runs from two thousand twenty-three, through two thousand twenty-four, into two thousand twenty-five.","时间线从 2023 年开始，经过 2024 年，一直到 2025 年。"],[175.51,182.78,99,"Look how fast the list grows, from the Emu and SEED families to Janus, Show-o, BAGEL and many more.","看看这份名单增长得多快，从 Emu 和 SEED 系列，到 Janus、Show-o、BAGEL 等等。"],[183.13,189.99,99,"And closed models like GPT-4o and Gemini two point oh Flash are in the race too.","像 GPT-4o 和 Gemini 2.0 Flash 这样的闭源模型也在这场竞赛中。"],[190.34,193.91,99,"The common goal: one model that can both see and draw.","共同的目标是：一个既能看、又能画的模型。"],[194.26,202.1,99,"And once a model can generate realistic images and videos, a bigger question appears: can it simulate a whole world?","而一旦模型能生成逼真的图像和视频，一个更大的问题就出现了：它能模拟整个世界吗？"],[203.35,210.78,100,"Let's try that in a domain we care a lot about: medicine. Medical Sora, towards a medical world simulator.","我们在一个非常关心的领域试试：医学。Medical Sora，迈向医学世界模拟器。"],[211.13,213.36,100,"Look at the range of scenarios.","看看这些场景的范围。"],[213.71,220.97,100,"Medical image analysis, like scrolling through CT slices, and medical care, like taping an injured shoulder.","医学影像分析，比如浏览 CT 切片；以及医疗护理，比如给受伤的肩膀贴扎。"],[221.32,226.8,100,"Instrument usage, like an MRI scanner, and even surgical operations.","器械使用，比如核磁共振扫描仪，甚至是外科手术。"],[227.15,235.64,100,"Medical popularization, like an animation of an injection, and medical scenarios, like a doctor talking to a patient.","医学科普，比如注射过程的动画；以及医疗场景，比如医生和病人交谈。"],[235.99,242.98,100,"Imagine training doctors, educating patients, or rehearsing a surgery, all inside a simulator.","想象一下，在模拟器里培训医生、教育患者，或者预演一场手术。"],[243.33,247.67,100,"A medical world simulator offers immense application potential.","医学世界模拟器有着巨大的应用潜力。"],[248.92,258.35,101,"And we can go even smaller, into the micro world. This is our work MicroVerse, a preliminary exploration toward micro-world simulation.","我们还可以走得更小，进入微观世界。这是我们的工作 MicroVerse，对微观世界模拟的初步探索。"],[258.7,265.48,101,"We give a prompt, like create a medical animation of human lung alveoli with capillaries and blood flow.","我们给出提示词，比如“制作一段人类肺泡及其毛细血管和血流的医学动画”。"],[265.83,270.74,101,"Then we compare a real video with videos generated by Sora and Veo3.","然后把真实视频与 Sora 和 Veo3 生成的视频进行比较。"],[271.09,281.45,101,"Three tasks: alveoli, cell division from one to two to four cells, and DNA turning into an RNA strand through polymerase.","三个任务：肺泡、细胞从一个分裂成两个再到四个，以及 DNA 通过聚合酶转录成 RNA 链。"],[281.8,287.08,101,"The videos look beautiful, but here's the real question: are they scientifically correct?","这些视频看起来很美，但真正的问题是：它们在科学上正确吗？"],[287.43,292.02,101,"Looking good is not the same as obeying the laws of biology and physics.","看起来好，并不等于遵守生物学和物理学规律。"],[292.37,297.28,101,"A true world simulator must get the rules of the world right, not just the pixels.","真正的世界模拟器必须把世界的规则做对，而不只是像素。"],[297.63,305.99,101,"And once a model can simulate the world, the next step is clear: an agent that acts in it. Let's meet embodied intelligence.","而一旦模型能模拟世界，下一步就很清楚了：一个在其中行动的智能体。让我们走进具身智能。"]]},{"n":7,"title":"Embodied Intelligence: VLA and World Models","blurb":"Vision-language-action models, System 1 and System 2, world models and world-action models.","file":"lecture10_part7.mp4","poster":"lecture10_part7.jpg","duration":633.7,"first":102,"last":110,"slides":[{"n":102,"title":"7 Embodied Intelligence: VLA and World Models","t":0.8},{"n":103,"title":"From Seeing to Acting: Why Embodiment Is Hard","t":25.71},{"n":104,"title":"Vision-Language-Action (VLA) Models","t":95.49},{"n":105,"title":"VLA Models: A Fast-Moving Timeline","t":178.97},{"n":106,"title":"System 2 Plans, System 1 Acts","t":252.58},{"n":107,"title":"A General Model as a Robot Brain? The Case of GPT-6 Astra","t":325.21},{"n":108,"title":"World Models: Learning How the World Changes","t":401.22},{"n":109,"title":"World-Action Models: Predict the Future and the Action Together","t":480.46},{"n":110,"title":"How Do We Improve Spatial Intelligence?","t":553.8}],"sents":[[0.8,6.4,102,"Part seven: embodied intelligence. This is where our models finally get a body!","第七部分：具身智能。在这里，我们的模型终于有了身体！"],[6.75,14.79,102,"To act in the physical world, a model must turn perception and language into motor commands, and predict what its actions will cause.","要在物理世界中行动，模型必须把感知和语言转化为运动指令，并预测自己的动作会带来什么后果。"],[15.14,24.31,102,"We will meet vision-language-action models, fast and slow thinking for robots, world models, world-action models, and spatial intelligence.","我们会认识视觉-语言-动作模型、机器人的快思考与慢思考、世界模型、世界-动作模型，以及空间智能。"],[25.56,30.93,103,"So why is acting so much harder than seeing? Start with Moravec's paradox.","那么，为什么行动比看懂难得多？先从莫拉维克悖论说起。"],[31.28,36.68,103,"What is hard for humans, like chess or calculus, turns out to be easy for AI.","对人类来说很难的事情，比如下棋或微积分，对 AI 来说反而很容易。"],[37.03,43.53,103,"But what is easy for a child, like folding laundry or pouring water, is really hard for a machine.","而对小孩来说很简单的事情，比如叠衣服、倒水，对机器来说却非常难。"],[43.88,50.21,103,"Here's my favorite way to put it: an LLM can explain how to make coffee, but it cannot make it.","我最喜欢这样说：大语言模型能讲清楚怎么做咖啡，却做不出一杯咖啡。"],[50.56,52.99,103,"The second problem is data.","第二个问题是数据。"],[53.34,57.08,103,"For text, we have roughly ten to the thirteen tokens on the web.","文本方面，网上大约有十的十三次方个 token。"],[57.43,67.75,103,"For robots, Open X-Embodiment in twenty twenty-three pooled about one million trajectories from twenty-two robot types, which is tiny by comparison.","机器人方面，2023 年的 Open X-Embodiment 汇集了来自 22 种机器人的约一百万条轨迹，相比之下微不足道。"],[68.1,71.8,103,"So there are three routes to physical intelligence.","所以，通往物理智能有三条路线。"],[72.15,79.05,103,"First, borrow web knowledge: start from a VLM and add an action head, which gives us a VLA.","第一，借用互联网知识：从一个 VLM 出发，加上动作头，就得到了 VLA。"],[79.4,86.67,103,"Second, learn physics from video by predicting the future, which leads to world models and world-action models.","第二，通过预测未来从视频中学习物理规律，这就引出了世界模型和世界-动作模型。"],[87.02,94.09,103,"And third, generate data with simulators and generated 3D worlds, which we will see in Part eight.","第三，用模拟器和生成的 3D 世界来生成数据，这部分我们会在第八部分看到。"],[95.34,102.93,104,"So, route one: the VLA. Its inputs are camera images and a language instruction, like: put the cup in the sink.","好，第一条路线：VLA。它的输入是相机图像和一条语言指令，比如：把杯子放进水槽。"],[103.28,110.63,104,"Both go into a VLM backbone pre-trained on the web, so the robot inherits all that world knowledge.","两者都送进一个在互联网数据上预训练的 VLM 主干，这样机器人就继承了所有这些世界知识。"],[110.98,120.45,104,"Then how do we get actions out? Design a uses action tokens: each joint value becomes one of two hundred fifty-six bins.","那动作怎么输出呢？方案 a 使用动作 token：每个关节值被离散化成 256 个区间之一。"],[120.8,127.05,104,"The model simply predicts them like words. That is RT-2 and OpenVLA.","模型就像预测单词一样预测它们。这就是 RT-2 和 OpenVLA。"],[127.4,138.82,104,"Design b adds an action expert trained with flow matching, which outputs fifty-step action chunks, as in pi zero, pi zero point five, and GR00T N1.","方案 b 加入一个用流匹配训练的动作专家，输出 50 步的动作块，比如 π0、π0.5 和 GR00T N1。"],[139.17,146.68,104,"Why did b win for dexterous control? First, actions are continuous and smooth, at around fifty hertz.","为什么在灵巧操作上 b 胜出了？第一，动作是连续、平滑的，频率大约 50 赫兹。"],[147.03,154.13,104,"Second, it can model multi-modal action distributions. Think of the many valid ways to grasp a cup.","第二，它能建模多峰的动作分布。想想抓起一个杯子有多少种正确的方式。"],[154.48,161.67,104,"Third, chunks predict half a second to one second of motion at once, so we call the slow VLM less often.","第三，动作块一次预测 0.5 到 1 秒的运动，所以调用慢速 VLM 的次数更少。"],[162.02,168.28,104,"For training, we co-train on web VQA plus robot data, so the model keeps its world knowledge.","训练时，我们把网络 VQA 数据和机器人数据一起联合训练，让模型保留它的世界知识。"],[168.63,177.57,104,"Then we pre-train across many robot bodies, fine-tune on tasks, and increasingly add reinforcement learning from real-world experience.","然后在多种机器人本体上预训练，再针对任务微调，而且越来越多地加入基于真实世界经验的强化学习。"],[178.82,183.13,105,"And this field is moving incredibly fast. Look at this timeline.","这个领域发展得极其迅速。看看这条时间线。"],[183.48,190.82,105,"July twenty twenty-three: RT-2 treats actions as text tokens, co-trained on web and robot data.","2023 年 7 月：RT-2 把动作当作文本 token，并用网络数据和机器人数据联合训练。"],[191.17,200.83,105,"June twenty twenty-four: OpenVLA, a seven-billion-parameter open model, trained on about nine hundred seventy thousand Open X-Embodiment episodes.","2024 年 6 月：OpenVLA，一个 70 亿参数的开源模型，在约 97 万条 Open X-Embodiment 数据上训练。"],[201.18,207.44,105,"October twenty twenty-four: pi zero introduces the flow-matching action expert.","2024 年 10 月：π0 提出了流匹配动作专家。"],[207.79,216.96,105,"March twenty twenty-five: Gemini Robotics brings a frontier VLM to robots, and GR00T N1 is a dual-system humanoid model.","2025 年 3 月：Gemini Robotics 把前沿 VLM 带到机器人上，GR00T N1 则是一个双系统的人形机器人模型。"],[217.31,223.93,105,"April twenty twenty-five: pi zero point five shows open-world generalization in new homes.","2025 年 4 月：π0.5 展示了在陌生家庭环境中的开放世界泛化能力。"],[224.28,238.1,105,"And in twenty twenty-six, GR00T N1.7, N2, and Gemini Robotics 2 push toward humanoid whole-body control, and N2 also predicts the next observation.","到了 2026 年，GR00T N1.7、N2 和 Gemini Robotics 2 推向人形机器人全身控制，而且 N2 还会预测下一帧观测。"],[238.45,247.14,105,"So the trend is clear: from discrete tokens to continuous action experts, and now toward models that also predict the future.","所以趋势很清楚：从离散 token 到连续的动作专家，现在又走向同时预测未来的模型。"],[247.49,251.18,105,"Keep that last point in mind, because it will come back very soon.","请记住最后这一点，因为它很快还会再出现。"],[252.43,259.54,106,"Now, a big design idea in robotics borrows from psychology: System 2 plans, System 1 acts.","接下来，机器人领域有一个借鉴心理学的重要设计思想：系统 2 负责规划，系统 1 负责执行。"],[259.89,270.28,106,"System 2 is the slow reasoner: a VLM or LLM that understands the scene, decomposes the task, and checks progress, at about one to ten hertz.","系统 2 是慢速推理者：一个 VLM 或 LLM，负责理解场景、分解任务、检查进度，频率大约 1 到 10 赫兹。"],[270.63,273.22,106,"It sends a subgoal to System 1.","它把子目标发送给系统 1。"],[273.57,281.78,106,"System 1 is the fast controller: a visuomotor policy that turns subgoals into motor commands, at fifty to two hundred hertz.","系统 1 是快速控制器：一个视觉运动策略，把子目标转化为运动指令，频率在 50 到 200 赫兹。"],[282.13,286.91,106,"And feedback from the robot flows back to System 2, along this dashed line.","机器人的反馈再沿着这条虚线回到系统 2。"],[287.26,292.95,106,"It is just like Kahneman's fast and slow thinking: you don't plan every finger movement when you pick up a cup.","这就像卡尼曼说的快思考与慢思考：你拿起杯子时，并不会去规划每一根手指的动作。"],[293.3,302.36,106,"For example, Figure Helix and NVIDIA GR00T N1 pair a seven-billion-scale VLM with a small fast policy.","举例来说，Figure Helix 和 NVIDIA GR00T N1 都是把一个 70 亿规模的 VLM 和一个小而快的策略组合起来。"],[302.71,311.65,106,"Google DeepMind pairs Gemini Robotics-ER for reasoning with Gemini Robotics for action, with version two in July twenty twenty-six.","Google DeepMind 用 Gemini Robotics-ER 负责推理，Gemini Robotics 负责动作，2026 年 7 月推出了第二版。"],[312.0,320.61,106,"And you can even plug in a generic frontier model as System 2, like GPT-6 Astra planning for a pi zero point five controller.","甚至可以把一个通用前沿模型当作系统 2，比如让 GPT-6 Astra 为 π0.5 控制器做规划。"],[320.96,323.81,106,"Does that actually work? Let's take a look.","这真的行得通吗？我们来看一看。"],[325.06,332.29,107,"So, can a general model be a robot brain? Let's take GPT-6 Astra as a case study.","那么，通用模型能当机器人的大脑吗？我们以 GPT-6 Astra 为例来看。"],[332.64,343.97,107,"It is an OpenAI frontier model released on September third, twenty twenty-six, launched for computer use, coding and science, not as a robotics model.","它是 OpenAI 在 2026 年 9 月 3 日发布的前沿模型，面向电脑操作、编程和科学研究，而不是机器人模型。"],[344.32,348.5,107,"But external researchers then tested it on robots.","但随后，外部研究者把它放到了机器人上测试。"],[348.85,356.49,107,"They report results on twelve embodied benchmarks: tabletop, humanoid, mobile, and dexterous hands.","他们在 12 个具身基准上报告了结果：桌面操作、人形机器人、移动机器人和灵巧手。"],[356.84,362.81,107,"It works best as System 2, in a closed loop with a fast System 1 like pi zero point five.","它最适合作为系统 2，与像 π0.5 这样的快速系统 1 组成闭环。"],[363.16,370.64,107,"Their verdict: it has crossed the threshold of embodied competence, but it is not yet practical embodied intelligence.","他们的结论是：它已经跨过了具身能力的门槛，但还不是实用的具身智能。"],[370.99,379.2,107,"So what does this mean? First, reasoning transfers: general models absorb spatial and task reasoning from scale.","这意味着什么？第一，推理能力可以迁移：通用模型通过规模吸收了空间推理和任务推理能力。"],[379.55,386.08,107,"Second, the bottleneck moves down, to low-level control, latency, and contact-rich skills.","第二，瓶颈往下移了，落到了底层控制、延迟和大量接触的操作技能上。"],[386.43,393.78,107,"And third, cost matters: demonstration cost and execution time still limit practical use.","第三，成本很重要：示范成本和执行时间仍然限制着实际应用。"],[394.13,399.82,107,"So reasoning alone is not enough. The model also needs to understand how the world changes.","所以光有推理还不够。模型还需要理解世界是如何变化的。"],[401.07,408.62,108,"That brings us to world models: a world model predicts the next state of the world, given the current state and an action.","这就引出了世界模型：世界模型根据当前状态和一个动作，预测世界的下一个状态。"],[408.97,414.2,108,"In symbols: s t plus one is approximately f of s t and a t.","用符号表示：s_{t+1} 约等于 f(s_t, a_t)。"],[414.55,419.67,108,"There are three flavors. First, generative video, which predicts pixels.","它有三种类型。第一种是生成式视频，直接预测像素。"],[420.02,428.72,108,"Genie 3 creates real-time interactive worlds with minutes of consistency, and NVIDIA Cosmos offers world foundation models for physical AI.","Genie 3 能生成实时交互的世界，并保持数分钟的一致性；NVIDIA Cosmos 则提供面向物理 AI 的世界基础模型。"],[429.07,436.14,108,"Second, latent predictive models, the JEPA family, which predict embeddings instead of pixels.","第二种是隐空间预测模型，也就是 JEPA 系列，它预测的是嵌入而不是像素。"],[436.49,446.03,108,"V-JEPA 2 is self-supervised on video, and its action-conditioned version, V-JEPA 2-AC, plans robot actions zero-shot.","V-JEPA 2 在视频上做自监督学习，它的动作条件版本 V-JEPA 2-AC 可以零样本规划机器人动作。"],[446.38,454.22,108,"Why embeddings? Because you can ignore unpredictable pixel details, like every leaf moving in the wind.","为什么用嵌入？因为这样可以忽略那些无法预测的像素细节，比如风中每一片树叶的晃动。"],[454.57,461.92,108,"Third, simulators for evaluation and data: use imagination as a test bed.","第三种是用于评测和数据的模拟器：把想象力当作试验场。"],[462.27,470.35,108,"Waymo builds driving scenarios on Genie 3, and Physical Intelligence evaluates robot policies inside world models.","Waymo 基于 Genie 3 构建驾驶场景，Physical Intelligence 则在世界模型里评测机器人策略。"],[470.7,479.06,108,"So the uses are: imagine before acting, train policies inside the dream, and test robots without breaking real ones.","所以它的用途是：行动之前先想象，在梦境中训练策略，以及在不弄坏真机器人的前提下测试机器人。"],[480.31,483.4,109,"Now let's put VLAs and world models together.","现在，我们把 VLA 和世界模型结合起来。"],[483.75,491.96,109,"A VLA maps observation and instruction to an action. It reacts, but has no explicit model of consequences.","VLA 把观测和指令映射为动作。它会做出反应，但没有显式地建模后果。"],[492.31,499.78,109,"A world model maps observation and action to the next observation. It imagines, but does not choose actions.","世界模型把观测和动作映射为下一帧观测。它会想象，但不会选择动作。"],[500.13,507.12,109,"A world-action model does both: from observation and instruction, it predicts future video plus actions.","世界-动作模型两者兼具：根据观测和指令，同时预测未来视频和动作。"],[507.47,510.48,109,"It imagines the outcome, and how to get there.","它既想象结果，也想象如何达到这个结果。"],[510.83,519.28,109,"There are two designs. Cascaded: a video model imagines the future, and an inverse-dynamics model reads off the actions.","有两种设计。级联式：视频模型想象未来，再由逆动力学模型从中读出动作。"],[519.63,524.05,109,"Or joint: one model learns video and actions together.","或者联合式：由一个模型同时学习视频和动作。"],[524.4,535.13,109,"Twenty twenty-six is full of examples. DreamZero, built on a video-diffusion backbone, reports more than double the generalization of VLAs.","2026 年有很多例子。DreamZero 基于视频扩散主干，报告的泛化能力是 VLA 的两倍以上。"],[535.48,544.78,109,"We also see GR00T N2, announced at GTC twenty twenty-six, plus AW-0 and GAWM in October.","还有在 GTC 2026 上发布的 GR00T N2，以及 10 月的 AW-0 和 GAWM。"],[545.13,552.4,109,"Why does it help? Video pre-training supplies a physics prior that scarce robot data alone cannot give.","为什么有效？因为视频预训练提供了物理先验，这是稀缺的机器人数据本身给不了的。"],[553.65,559.29,110,"Underneath all of this sits one big question: how do we improve spatial intelligence?","这一切背后都有一个大问题：我们如何提升空间智能？"],[559.64,571.18,110,"Today's MLLMs read images well, but reason about space poorly: metric distance, mental rotation, counting in 3D, and egocentric versus allocentric views.","如今的多模态大模型看图很在行，但空间推理很差：度量距离、心理旋转、3D 计数，以及自我中心与他者中心视角的转换。"],[571.53,580.18,110,"Here are six levers. Data: 3D-grounded QA from scans and simulators, and egocentric video with camera poses.","这里有六个抓手。数据：来自扫描和模拟器的 3D 落地问答，以及带相机位姿的第一人称视频。"],[580.53,589.67,110,"Representation: add geometry, like 3D tokens, depth, or features from 3D foundation models such as VGGT.","表示：加入几何信息，比如 3D token、深度，或者来自 VGGT 等 3D 基础模型的特征。"],[590.02,596.2,110,"Memory: keep an explicit 3D map of what was seen, instead of a bag of frames.","记忆：为看到过的内容保存一张显式的 3D 地图，而不是一堆零散的帧。"],[596.55,602.68,110,"Objectives: predict depth, motion and the next view, not only the next word.","目标函数：预测深度、运动和下一个视角，而不只是下一个词。"],[603.03,609.61,110,"Reasoning: think with images, so sketch, crop, and re-render views while reasoning.","推理：用图像思考，在推理过程中画草图、裁剪、重新渲染视角。"],[609.96,616.33,110,"And embodiment: learn by acting, with physical outcomes as the reward.","还有具身：在行动中学习，把物理结果当作奖励。"],[616.68,625.78,110,"Our view: spatial intelligence will come from closing the loop. Perceive, reconstruct, imagine, act, verify.","我们的观点是：空间智能将来自闭环。感知、重建、想象、行动、验证。"],[626.13,631.86,110,"And to reconstruct and imagine, we need 3D. That is our next part.","而要重建和想象，我们就需要 3D。这就是下一部分的内容。"]]},{"n":8,"title":"3D Understanding and Generation","blurb":"Reconstruction, 3D generation, and language-driven 3D scene building.","file":"lecture10_part8.mp4","poster":"lecture10_part8.jpg","duration":371.0,"first":111,"last":116,"slides":[{"n":111,"title":"8 3D Understanding and Generation","t":0.8},{"n":112,"title":"Why 3D? Images Are Only Projections","t":19.92},{"n":113,"title":"3D Reconstruction: From Hours of Optimization to One Forward Pass","t":86.76},{"n":114,"title":"3D Generation: Objects and Worlds","t":163.49},{"n":115,"title":"Language-Driven 3D: The LLM as a Scene Programmer","t":233.45},{"n":116,"title":"Thinking Ahead: What Should Future Models Do in 3D?","t":306.53}],"sents":[[0.8,4.05,111,"Part eight: 3D understanding and generation.","第八部分：3D 理解与生成。"],[4.4,10.41,111,"Here's a simple but deep fact: every image is just a projection of a 3D world.","这是一个简单而深刻的事实：每一张图像都只是三维世界的一个投影。"],[10.76,18.52,111,"So reconstructing, understanding and generating 3D is the foundation of spatial intelligence. Let's dig in!","所以，重建、理解和生成 3D，是空间智能的基础。我们深入看看！"],[19.77,27.41,112,"Why 3D? Because when a camera takes a picture, depth gets flattened away. Images are only projections.","为什么要 3D？因为相机拍照时，深度被压扁了。图像只是投影。"],[27.76,33.29,112,"So first, how do we even represent 3D? Here are five common choices.","那么首先，3D 到底怎么表示？这里有五种常见的选择。"],[33.64,39.65,112,"A point cloud is just unordered x y z points, the kind of data you get from LiDAR.","点云就是一堆无序的 xyz 点，激光雷达得到的就是这类数据。"],[40.0,47.07,112,"A mesh stores vertices and faces, and it is used in games, CAD, and 3D printing.","网格存储顶点和面，用于游戏、CAD 和 3D 打印。"],[47.42,54.77,112,"A NeRF is a neural network that maps a position and a viewing direction to color, giving photorealistic views.","NeRF 是一个神经网络，把位置和观察方向映射为颜色，能渲染出照片级真实的视角。"],[55.12,61.66,112,"3D Gaussian splatting uses millions of soft 3D blobs, and it renders in real time.","3D 高斯泼溅用数百万个柔和的 3D 小团块来表示场景，并且可以实时渲染。"],[62.01,68.74,112,"And structured latents are a voxel grid of learned features, used for 3D generation.","结构化隐变量则是由学习到的特征组成的体素网格，用于 3D 生成。"],[69.09,78.63,112,"So there are two directions with one goal: reconstruct 3D from images, which is understanding, and create 3D from text or images, which is generation.","所以是两个方向、一个目标：从图像重建 3D，这是理解；从文本或图像创建 3D，这是生成。"],[78.98,85.36,112,"Robots, AR and VR, games, digital twins, and spatial reasoning all need both.","机器人、AR 和 VR、游戏、数字孪生以及空间推理，全都同时需要这两者。"],[86.61,93.88,113,"Let's start with reconstruction, where something remarkable happened: from hours of optimization to one forward pass.","先看重建。这里发生了一件了不起的事：从数小时的优化，变成了一次前向计算。"],[94.23,98.49,113,"The classic pipeline is Structure-from-Motion, like COLMAP.","经典流程是运动恢复结构，比如 COLMAP。"],[98.84,107.13,113,"You extract features, match them across images, estimate camera poses, and refine everything with bundle adjustment.","先提取特征，在图像间做匹配，估计相机位姿，再用光束法平差整体优化。"],[107.48,111.57,113,"Finally, dense multi-view stereo fills in the details.","最后，用稠密多视图立体把细节补全。"],[111.92,118.54,113,"It takes minutes to hours, and it is fragile with few views, low texture, or motion.","这需要几分钟到几小时，而且在视角少、纹理弱或有运动时很脆弱。"],[118.89,125.07,113,"The learned approach is radically simpler: a single network predicts the geometry.","基于学习的方法则简单得多：一个网络直接预测几何。"],[125.42,135.86,113,"Feed in one to N images, run a Transformer in one forward pass, and get camera poses, depth maps, point maps and point tracks, in under a second!","输入 1 到 N 张图像，Transformer 只做一次前向计算，就能在一秒以内得到相机位姿、深度图、点图和点轨迹！"],[136.21,144.45,113,"DUSt3R, at CVPR twenty twenty-four, predicts aligned point maps from an image pair, with no calibration needed.","CVPR 2024 的 DUSt3R 从一对图像预测对齐的点图，不需要相机标定。"],[144.8,154.83,113,"And VGGT, the CVPR twenty twenty-five best paper, predicts all 3D attributes from one to hundreds of views, feed-forward.","而 CVPR 2025 最佳论文 VGGT，能从一张到数百张视图中，前馈式地预测所有 3D 属性。"],[155.18,162.09,113,"It's the same story we saw in NLP: a hand-built pipeline replaced by one big pre-trained model.","这和我们在 NLP 里看到的故事一样：手工搭建的流水线被一个大型预训练模型取代。"],[163.34,169.22,114,"Now the other direction: 3D generation, for both objects and whole worlds.","再看另一个方向：3D 生成，既包括物体，也包括整个世界。"],[169.57,173.8,114,"For objects, one approach is multi-view then reconstruct.","对于物体，一种方法是先生成多视图再重建。"],[174.15,181.06,114,"A 2D diffusion model draws consistent views, and a reconstruction model lifts them to 3D.","先用 2D 扩散模型画出一致的多个视角，再用重建模型把它们提升到 3D。"],[181.41,189.33,114,"A second approach runs diffusion directly in a native 3D latent space, like TRELLIS and Hunyuan3D 2.0.","第二种方法直接在原生 3D 隐空间中做扩散，比如 TRELLIS 和 Hunyuan3D 2.0。"],[189.68,198.25,114,"And SAM 3D from Meta, in November twenty twenty-five, reconstructs objects and human bodies from a single photo.","还有 Meta 在 2025 年 11 月推出的 SAM 3D，能从一张照片重建物体和人体。"],[198.6,209.39,114,"For whole worlds, World Labs Marble creates persistent, navigable 3D worlds from text, images, or video, stored as Gaussian splats.","对于整个世界，World Labs 的 Marble 能从文本、图像或视频生成持久、可漫游的 3D 世界，以高斯泼溅的形式存储。"],[209.74,214.86,114,"And Genie 3 generates interactive worlds frame by frame, explorable in real time.","而 Genie 3 则逐帧生成可交互的世界，可以实时探索。"],[215.21,225.65,114,"Here's the key distinction: explicit 3D, which you can measure and simulate, versus pixels that only look 3D, where consistency is not guaranteed.","关键区别在于：显式 3D 可以测量、可以仿真；而只是看起来像 3D 的像素，无法保证一致性。"],[226.0,232.05,114,"For robots and engineering, we need the former. For media, the latter is often enough.","对机器人和工程来说，我们需要前者；对媒体内容来说，后者往往就够了。"],[233.3,239.31,115,"So what role does the language model play in 3D? It can be a scene programmer.","那么，语言模型在 3D 中扮演什么角色？它可以当一个场景程序员。"],[239.66,245.92,115,"Start with a prompt: a cozy reading room, two armchairs facing the window, a lamp between them.","从一句提示开始：一间温馨的阅读室，两把扶手椅面朝窗户，中间放一盏灯。"],[246.27,252.24,115,"The LLM plans a scene graph and layout: which objects, their sizes, and their relations.","LLM 规划出场景图和布局：有哪些物体、它们的尺寸以及彼此的关系。"],[252.59,261.56,115,"Then we retrieve or generate each 3D asset, solve the constraints with a physics check, and get a simulator-ready 3D scene.","然后检索或生成每一个 3D 资产，求解约束并做物理检查，得到一个可直接用于模拟器的 3D 场景。"],[261.91,265.65,115,"Look at the intermediate representation the LLM writes.","看看 LLM 写出的中间表示。"],[266.0,275.54,115,"Objects: two armchairs and a floor lamp. Relations: chair one faces the window, and the lamp sits between the two chairs.","物体：两把扶手椅和一盏落地灯。关系：一号椅子面朝窗户，灯位于两把椅子之间。"],[275.89,283.7,115,"Notice the division of labor: language is great at this kind of structure, while the solver handles the precise geometry.","注意这里的分工：语言擅长表达这种结构，而精确的几何交给求解器处理。"],[284.05,290.06,115,"Holodeck uses this idea to generate 3D environments for training embodied agents.","Holodeck 就用这个思路生成 3D 环境，用来训练具身智能体。"],[290.41,298.36,115,"3D-LLM and ShapeLLM go the other way: they are language models that read point clouds.","3D-LLM 和 ShapeLLM 则反过来：它们是能读懂点云的语言模型。"],[298.71,305.13,115,"And in twenty twenty-six, agentic scene builders write code directly in Blender or simulators.","到了 2026 年，智能体式的场景构建器会直接在 Blender 或模拟器里写代码。"],[306.38,313.0,116,"Let's close this part by thinking ahead. What should future models do in 3D? I see five things.","最后，我们往前看一看。未来的模型在 3D 方面应该做什么？我认为有五点。"],[313.35,322.78,116,"One: a single world representation, the same 3D-consistent latent for understanding, generation, and action.","第一：统一的世界表示，用同一个 3D 一致的隐表示来做理解、生成和行动。"],[323.13,331.42,116,"Two: executable worlds. Generated scenes must be simulatable, so generation becomes a data engine for robots.","第二：可执行的世界。生成的场景必须可以仿真，这样生成就成了机器人的数据引擎。"],[331.77,339.2,116,"Three: language as interface, geometry as substrate. Talk in words, compute in 3D.","第三：语言作为接口，几何作为基底。用语言交流，在 3D 中计算。"],[339.55,346.28,116,"Four: close the loop. Perceive, reconstruct, imagine, act, verify, continuously.","第四：形成闭环。感知、重建、想象、行动、验证，持续不断地循环。"],[346.63,354.92,116,"Five: evaluate by doing. The best test of a 3D world model is whether an agent trained in it succeeds in reality.","第五：在实践中评估。检验一个 3D 世界模型的最好标准，是在其中训练的智能体能否在现实中成功。"],[355.27,361.89,116,"Language models learned the world from text. The next models must learn it from space, time, and action.","语言模型从文本中认识世界；下一代模型必须从空间、时间和行动中认识世界。"],[362.24,369.15,116,"And that brings us to the bigger picture: what are the open research directions for multimodal AI? Let's look ahead.","这也把我们带到更大的图景：多模态 AI 还有哪些开放的研究方向？我们一起往前看。"]]},{"n":9,"title":"Research Directions and Outlook","blurb":"Efficiency, evaluation, edge devices, what changed in 2026, and closing remarks.","file":"lecture10_part9.mp4","poster":"lecture10_part9.jpg","duration":660.2,"first":117,"last":134,"slides":[{"n":117,"title":"9 Research Directions and Outlook","t":0.8},{"n":118,"title":"Efficient multimodal MLLMs:","t":17.39},{"n":119,"title":"Generating multimodal outputs (vision, action, etc.)","t":83.16},{"n":120,"title":"Vertical Applications (e.g. medical applications)","t":130.88},{"n":121,"title":"Evaluations","t":178.28},{"n":122,"title":"Incorporating more data modalities","t":231.22},{"n":123,"title":"Video Understanding and Multimodal Reasoning","t":270.76},{"n":124,"title":"Edge-device Multi-modal LLMs","t":319.52},{"n":125,"title":"MLLMs for Edge devices","t":332.98},{"n":126,"title":"A naïve demo","t":359.37},{"n":127,"title":"Multimodal AI in 2026: What Changed","t":383.23},{"n":128,"title":"Final remarks from multi-modal interactions","t":454.47},{"n":129,"title":"Why We Need Multimodal LLMs","t":465.2},{"n":130,"title":"Adobe Firefly turns Photoshop into effortless AI image generator","t":506.92},{"n":131,"title":"Final remarks","t":533.57},{"n":132,"title":"Final projects","t":568.31},{"n":133,"title":"AIMO 3 is coming","t":586.85},{"n":134,"title":"Acknowledgement","t":611.62}],"sents":[[0.8,5.63,117,"Okay! Part nine, our final part: research directions and outlook.","好！第九部分，也是最后一部分：研究方向与展望。"],[5.98,10.08,117,"We have built a lot today, but the field is far from finished.","今天我们已经搭建了很多东西，但这个领域还远没有结束。"],[10.43,15.99,117,"So let's look at where multimodal AI is going, and what is still open for you to work on.","所以我们来看看多模态 AI 正在走向哪里，以及还有哪些问题留给你们去研究。"],[17.24,23.16,118,"First direction: efficiency. Multimodal models are expensive, so how do we make them cheaper?","第一个方向：效率。多模态模型很昂贵，我们怎样让它更便宜？"],[23.51,31.35,118,"One idea is a simple projection, like Fuyu, which feeds image patches almost directly into the language model.","一种思路是简单的投影，比如 Fuyu，它几乎直接把图像块送进语言模型。"],[31.7,38.4,118,"Another idea is token reduction: images produce a huge number of tokens, so we keep fewer of them.","另一种思路是减少 token：图像会产生大量 token，那我们就少保留一些。"],[38.75,45.82,118,"Our own work, Less is More, shows that a simple token reduction method can work surprisingly well.","我们自己的工作 Less is More 表明，一个简单的 token 削减方法就能取得出乎意料的好效果。"],[46.17,55.83,118,"Then there is parameter-efficient tuning. Look at LLaMA-Adapter V2: the LLM stays frozen, and only small adapters are trained.","然后是参数高效微调。看 LLaMA-Adapter V2：大模型保持冻结，只训练一些小的适配器。"],[56.18,59.18,118,"That is only fourteen million trainable parameters!","可训练参数只有一千四百万！"],[59.53,66.15,118,"LAVIN goes even further, with a mixture-of-modality adapter, and just three point eight million parameters.","LAVIN 更进一步，采用多模态混合适配器，只有三百八十万个参数。"],[66.5,74.5,118,"And with QLoRA, you can finetune a sixty-five billion parameter LLaMA in twenty-four hours on a single GPU.","而借助 QLoRA，你可以在单张 GPU 上用二十四小时微调一个六百五十亿参数的 LLaMA。"],[74.85,81.76,118,"It reaches ninety-nine point three percent of ChatGPT's performance level. Efficiency really matters.","它达到了 ChatGPT 性能水平的百分之九十九点三。效率真的很重要。"],[83.01,87.79,119,"Second direction: generating multimodal outputs, not just reading them.","第二个方向：生成多模态输出，而不只是读取它们。"],[88.14,95.17,119,"This paper by Koh and colleagues shows a language model that can generate and retrieve images, together with text.","Koh 等人的这篇论文展示了一个语言模型，它能在生成文字的同时，生成和检索图像。"],[95.52,105.14,119,"Look at the dialogue. The user thinks of an animal, the model guesses a beaver, and then the user asks for a pencil drawing, and a comic version.","看这段对话。用户想着一种动物，模型猜出是河狸，接着用户要一张铅笔画，再要一张漫画版。"],[105.49,111.34,119,"Their model decides by itself when to retrieve an image and when to generate a new one.","他们的模型能自己决定什么时候检索图像，什么时候生成一张新图。"],[111.69,116.36,119,"FROMAGe can only retrieve, so it is limited to existing images.","FROMAGe 只能检索，所以只能用已有的图像。"],[116.71,122.92,119,"And Stable Diffusion can only generate, and it struggles with long dialogue context.","而 Stable Diffusion 只能生成，并且很难处理长的对话上下文。"],[123.27,129.48,119,"And as the title says, the same idea extends beyond images, to actions as well.","正如标题所说，同样的思路也可以从图像扩展到动作。"],[130.73,135.64,120,"Third direction: vertical applications, and medicine is a great example.","第三个方向：垂直领域应用，医疗就是一个很好的例子。"],[135.99,142.9,120,"There are pathology assistants like PathAsst, medical visual question answering like PMC-VQA, and LLaVA-Med.","有像 PathAsst 这样的病理助手，有 PMC-VQA 这样的医学视觉问答，还有 LLaVA-Med。"],[143.25,147.67,120,"LLaVA-Med starts from the general LLaVA model and adapts it in two stages.","LLaVA-Med 从通用的 LLaVA 模型出发，分两个阶段进行适配。"],[148.02,155.83,120,"Stage one aligns medical concepts in seven hours, and stage two does medical instruction tuning in eight hours.","第一阶段用七个小时对齐医学概念，第二阶段用八个小时做医学指令微调。"],[156.18,160.0,120,"That is why the title says: trained in one day!","这就是为什么标题说：一天之内训练完成！"],[160.35,163.43,120,"Now compare the answers about this CT scan.","现在对比一下关于这张 CT 片子的回答。"],[163.78,168.81,120,"LLaVA-Med correctly describes the scan and points out a large pelvic mass.","LLaVA-Med 正确描述了这张片子，并指出了一个较大的盆腔肿块。"],[169.16,176.88,120,"The general LLaVA, in red, misreads the image and cannot find the abnormality. Domain knowledge matters.","而通用的 LLaVA，红字部分，看错了图像，也找不出异常。领域知识很重要。"],[178.13,182.6,121,"Fourth direction: evaluation. How do we know these models really work?","第四个方向：评测。我们怎么知道这些模型真的有效？"],[182.95,191.16,121,"People study object hallucination, adversarial robustness, OCR ability, and build benchmarks like LAMM.","大家研究物体幻觉、对抗鲁棒性、OCR 能力，还构建了像 LAMM 这样的基准。"],[191.51,199.72,121,"On the left, notice how different the training data is, from about half a million samples for LLaVA to over a billion for mPLUG-Owl.","看左边，各模型的训练数据量差别很大，从 LLaVA 的约六十万样本，到 mPLUG-Owl 的超过十亿。"],[200.07,209.29,121,"Now the table. On OCR, the best multimodal model scores about sixty-four, while supervised state of the art is about eighty-five.","再看表格。在 OCR 上，最好的多模态模型约六十四分，而有监督的最好方法约八十五分。"],[209.64,217.39,121,"When OCR needs reasoning too, the best model gets only sixteen, against seventy-three. A huge gap!","当 OCR 还需要推理时，最好的模型只有十六分，而对比是七十三分。差距巨大！"],[217.74,224.69,121,"Look at this example: what is the cheapest fruit? You must read the price tags and then compare them.","看这个例子：最便宜的水果是什么？你必须先读出价签，再进行比较。"],[225.04,229.82,121,"So good evaluation shows us exactly where our models still fail.","所以好的评测能准确告诉我们，模型在哪里仍然会失败。"],[231.07,234.64,122,"Fifth direction: incorporating more data modalities.","第五个方向：引入更多的数据模态。"],[234.99,241.41,122,"Today most systems handle text and images, but we also want videos, music, and 3D.","今天大多数系统处理文字和图像，但我们还希望处理视频、音乐和 3D。"],[241.76,248.86,122,"Wouldn't it be amazing to have one shared embedding space for all modalities? That is exactly the idea of ImageBind.","如果所有模态共享一个嵌入空间，那该多好？这正是 ImageBind 的思路。"],[249.21,256.76,122,"It aligns six modalities, so the crackle of a fire can retrieve fire images, depth maps, and text.","它对齐了六种模态，所以火焰的噼啪声可以检索到火的图像、深度图和文字。"],[257.11,262.96,122,"You can even do arithmetic: a bird image plus the sound of waves gives you birds by the sea.","你甚至可以做向量运算：一张鸟的图片，加上海浪的声音，就得到了海边的鸟。"],[263.31,269.36,122,"And you can generate images directly from audio, like a dog barking or rain falling.","你还可以直接从音频生成图像，比如狗叫或者下雨。"],[270.61,274.95,123,"Sixth direction: video understanding and multimodal reasoning.","第六个方向：视频理解与多模态推理。"],[275.3,282.94,123,"Videos are long. LongLLaVA uses a hybrid of Mamba and Transformer to process more than a thousand images efficiently.","视频很长。LongLLaVA 采用 Mamba 和 Transformer 的混合架构，高效处理一千多张图像。"],[283.29,289.26,123,"VideoLLaVA and LLaVA-OneVision extend image models to video with temporal modeling.","VideoLLaVA 和 LLaVA-OneVision 通过时序建模，把图像模型扩展到视频。"],[289.61,296.63,123,"And remember reinforcement learning for reasoning from Lecture eight-one? It now comes to multimodal models.","还记得第八讲第一部分里用强化学习做推理吗？它现在也来到了多模态模型。"],[296.98,306.25,123,"Video-R1 uses RL for video reasoning, and tests whether models really care about frame order, by shuffling the frames.","Video-R1 用强化学习做视频推理，并通过打乱帧顺序，检验模型是否真正在意帧的先后。"],[306.6,310.78,123,"Visual chain-of-thought brings step-by-step reasoning to images.","视觉思维链把一步一步的推理带到了图像上。"],[311.13,318.12,123,"And benchmarks like MathVista and MMMU test math, science, and graduate-level questions.","而 MathVista 和 MMMU 这样的基准，考察数学、科学和研究生水平的问题。"],[319.37,325.38,124,"Now, a topic close to my heart: multimodal LLMs on edge devices.","接下来是我特别关心的一个话题：端侧多模态大模型。"],[325.73,331.58,124,"What if the model does not live in a huge data center, but right in your hand?","如果模型不是住在巨大的数据中心里，而是就在你的手上，会怎样？"],[332.83,337.21,125,"Here is the goal: running on edge devices, with streaming capability.","目标是：在端侧设备上运行，并且具备流式处理能力。"],[337.56,343.08,125,"Look at this board. It is a Raspberry Pi 5, a tiny and cheap computer.","看这块板子。这是一台 Raspberry Pi 5，一台小巧又便宜的电脑。"],[343.43,346.39,125,"It is not much bigger than the SD card next to it!","它比旁边那张 SD 卡也大不了多少！"],[346.74,352.55,125,"Running a model here means no cloud, lower latency, and your data stays private.","在这里运行模型，就意味着不依赖云端、延迟更低，而且数据留在本地，保护隐私。"],[352.9,357.97,125,"The hard part is fitting a multimodal model into such limited memory and compute.","难点在于，如何把多模态模型塞进如此有限的内存和算力里。"],[359.22,362.43,126,"And here is a naive demo.","这是一个简单的演示。"],[362.78,367.93,126,"On the whiteboard it says, in Chinese: on-device multimodal large models.","白板上用中文写着：端侧多模态大模型。"],[368.28,374.82,126,"Notice the small device in his hand. It carries a camera, and the model runs right there, on the edge.","注意他手里的小设备。它带着摄像头，模型就直接在端侧运行。"],[375.17,381.83,126,"It is simple, but it shows the future: multimodal assistants that live in small, everyday devices.","它很简单，但展示了未来：住在日常小设备里的多模态助手。"],[383.08,388.24,127,"Now let's zoom out. What changed in multimodal AI in two thousand twenty-six?","现在我们把视角拉远。二〇二六年，多模态 AI 发生了哪些变化？"],[388.59,397.64,127,"First, omni is the default: real-time speech plus vision models, like Qwen three point five Omni in April, and full-duplex systems.","第一，全模态成了默认：实时的语音加视觉模型，比如四月发布的 Qwen3.5-Omni，还有全双工的研究系统。"],[397.99,405.07,127,"Second, world models became products, from Genie 3 to the Waymo World Model, and World Labs' World API.","第二，世界模型变成了产品，从 Genie 3 到 Waymo World Model，还有 World Labs 的 World API。"],[405.42,413.05,127,"Third, from VLA to world-action models: DreamZero and Groot N2 predict the future, not only the action.","第三，从 VLA 走向世界-动作模型：DreamZero 和 GR00T N2 不仅预测动作，还预测未来。"],[413.4,422.34,127,"Fourth, general models go physical, with GPT-6 Astra evaluated as a robot planner, and Gemini Robotics 2.","第四，通用模型走向物理世界：GPT-6 Astra 被当作机器人规划器来评测，还有 Gemini Robotics 2。"],[422.69,431.39,127,"Fifth, 3D in one forward pass: feed-forward reconstruction and native 3D generation are now standard tools.","第五，一次前向就得到 3D：前馈式重建和原生 3D 生成已经成为标准工具。"],[431.74,437.46,127,"Notice how these trends match our journey today: talk, imagine, act, and understand space.","注意，这些趋势正好对应我们今天的旅程：说、想象、行动和理解空间。"],[437.81,448.09,127,"And here are the open problems for you: data for physical interaction, evaluation of interaction, efficient always-on models, and safety of acting agents.","这些是留给你们的开放问题：物理交互的数据、交互的评测、高效的常开模型，以及行动智能体的安全。"],[448.44,453.07,127,"Any of these could become your final project, or even your PhD thesis!","其中任何一个，都可能成为你的期末项目，甚至你的博士论文！"],[454.32,460.24,128,"Finally, let me share some final remarks, from the angle of multimodal interaction.","最后，我想从多模态交互的角度，分享几点结束语。"],[460.59,463.8,128,"Why does all of this matter for real people?","这一切对真实的人来说，为什么重要？"],[465.05,468.01,129,"So why do we need multimodal LLMs?","那么，我们为什么需要多模态大模型？"],[468.36,475.9,129,"First, speech is more convenient for interaction. Talking is easier than typing, especially for many patients.","第一，语音交互更方便。说话比打字容易，对很多病人来说尤其如此。"],[476.25,482.79,129,"You can see this in our HuatuoGPT applications, where users simply talk to the medical model.","你可以在我们的 HuatuoGPT 应用中看到这一点，用户直接和医疗模型对话就行。"],[483.14,486.39,129,"Second, video is language-agnostic.","第二，视频是不依赖语言的。"],[486.74,491.98,129,"You can enjoy a funny TikTok video from India without understanding the language at all.","你可以欣赏一段来自印度的有趣 TikTok 视频，哪怕完全听不懂那里的语言。"],[492.33,498.99,129,"Third, and this is the key point: data in other modalities needs a language interface to interact with.","第三，也是最关键的一点：其他模态的数据，需要一个语言接口来进行交互。"],[499.34,505.52,129,"For example, you can now draw just by describing what you want, with language-based AI tools.","比如，现在借助基于语言接口的 AI 工具，你只要描述想要什么，就能画出来。"],[506.77,510.74,130,"Here is exactly that: Adobe Firefly inside Photoshop.","这正是一个例子：Photoshop 里的 Adobe Firefly。"],[511.09,515.23,130,"You select a region of the photo, here a patch of the empty road.","你在照片上选出一块区域，这里是空旷路面的一部分。"],[515.58,520.95,130,"Then you simply describe what you would like to generate, and click Generate.","然后你只需描述想生成什么，再点击 Generate。"],[521.3,526.42,130,"The result appears as a new layer, so the original photo is untouched.","结果会作为一个新图层出现，原图保持不变。"],[526.77,532.17,130,"No brushes, no years of training. Language becomes the interface to images.","不需要画笔，也不需要多年的训练。语言成了操作图像的接口。"],[533.42,536.75,131,"And here is my final remark, with a dream.","这是我最后的一点感想，也是一个梦想。"],[537.1,544.94,131,"On the left is a human, shown as an avatar. On the right is an agent, and everything you see there is generated.","左边是一个人，以虚拟形象出现。右边是一个智能体，你在那里看到的一切都是生成的。"],[545.29,553.01,131,"In the clip, the agent sits at a table with a cup, moving and responding naturally, like a real person on a video call.","在这段视频里，这个智能体坐在放着杯子的桌前，动作和回应都很自然，就像视频通话里的真人。"],[553.36,560.67,131,"It has to see, listen, talk, and act, all at once. That is every topic of today in one system.","它必须同时去看、去听、去说、去行动。这就是把今天所有的主题融进了一个系统。"],[561.02,566.91,131,"So I hope, one day, AI could finally pass the Turing test in a video interaction!","所以我希望，有一天，AI 能在视频交互中最终通过图灵测试！"],[568.16,571.9,132,"Before we wrap up, a quick note about your final projects.","在结束之前，简单说一下你们的期末项目。"],[572.25,577.37,132,"Next week, I will hold ad hoc Starbucks time every day at noon.","下周，我每天中午都会有一个临时的星巴克时间。"],[577.72,581.54,132,"The tentative time is twelve thirty to one pm.","暂定时间是中午十二点半到一点。"],[581.89,585.45,132,"Just come by with your ideas, and let's chat over coffee!","带着你的想法过来就行，我们边喝咖啡边聊！"],[586.7,594.34,133,"And one more opportunity: AIMO 3, the AI Mathematical Olympiad Progress Prize 3, on Kaggle.","还有一个机会：AIMO 3，也就是 Kaggle 上的人工智能数学奥林匹克进步奖第三届。"],[594.69,599.68,133,"The goal is to build open-source models that solve olympiad-level math problems.","目标是构建能够解出奥赛级数学题的开源模型。"],[600.03,604.91,133,"And look at the prize: more than two point two million US dollars!","再看看奖金：超过两百二十万美元！"],[605.26,610.22,133,"If you enjoyed our lecture on reasoning models, this is a great place to test your skills.","如果你喜欢我们讲推理模型的那一讲，这里是检验你能力的好地方。"],[611.47,617.16,134,"Finally, many thanks to these excellent resources, which inspired parts of today's lecture.","最后，非常感谢这些优秀的资料，今天的课有一部分内容受到了它们的启发。"],[617.51,620.09,134,"Let's look back at our journey today.","让我们回顾一下今天的旅程。"],[620.44,627.71,134,"We taught models to see with CLIP and Flamingo, and to talk about images with multimodal LLMs.","我们用 CLIP 和 Flamingo 教模型去看，又用多模态大模型教它们谈论图像。"],[628.06,634.84,134,"We taught them to hear and speak with speech language models, and to imagine with generation and world simulators.","我们用语音语言模型教它们去听和说，用生成模型和世界模拟器教它们去想象。"],[635.19,641.57,134,"Then we taught them to act as embodied agents, and finally to understand space in 3D.","接着我们教它们作为具身智能体去行动，最后去理解三维空间。"],[641.92,650.61,134,"See, talk, hear and speak, imagine, act, and understand space. That is the road to truly multimodal AI.","看、说、听与讲、想象、行动、理解空间。这就是通往真正多模态 AI 的道路。"],[650.96,655.03,134,"And remember, many of the open problems are waiting for you.","记住，还有很多开放问题在等着你们。"],[655.38,658.3,134,"Thank you all for listening, and see you next time!","谢谢大家的聆听，我们下次见！"]]}]};
